d themselves with HTTP Basic authentication, which\nthe GraphQL switch removed. They described a system that no longer exists, in\nthe files most likely to be read during a security review.\n\nThe substantive correction is why an internal host is refused. Utils.getHostName\nsaid the render request built from that host carries Basic credentials, so a\nprivate address had to be rejected to prevent SSRF. Nothing is fetched from that\nhost any more - rendering goes to the local GraphQL endpoint - so the host is\nonly ever the citation URL stored in CustomGPT. The guard still earns its place,\nfor a different reason: a citation nobody outside the network can open is worse\nthan no citation. Same for normalizeServerName, which repeated the credential\nrationale twice, including for its https default.\n\nAlso:\n\n- the class javadoc listed \"the Jahia rendering password and the server-cookie\n  value\" among the write-only secrets; neither exists. It names the CustomGPT\n  token and the Jahia API token.\n- isHttpsUrl claimed to gate the Jahia rendering URL. It never does - its only\n  caller is the CustomGPT apiBaseUrl check.\n- okhttp3.Credentials was imported by CustomGptIndexerNodeHandler and unused.\n  Java does not fail on an unused import, so it survived the removal of the\n  Basic-auth code it belonged to.\n\nThe log line now says \"Refusing to index\" rather than \"Refusing to render\" and\nstates the consequence, since skipping is no longer about rendering at all.\n\nThe two Basic-auth mentions left in JahiaRenderClient are deliberate: they\nrecord what this class replaced.\n\nNo behaviour change: comments, one dead import, one log string. 341 tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"48da4e91246a4aeea6f2dde5242598c7c650b464","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/48da4e91246a4aeea6f2dde5242598c7c650b464"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/f7a8eb2aea1894f0640afd8b8c176c9105cb3f19","verification":{"payload":"tree 48da4e91246a4aeea6f2dde5242598c7c650b464\nparent c2aaffb0758dbe1e5f6e450757cfe01b0fa53ca0\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791451442 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791451442 +0200\n\ndocs: correct the comments describing how the render request authenticates\n\nEight comments still justified themselves with HTTP Basic authentication, which\nthe GraphQL switch removed. They described a system that no longer exists, in\nthe files most likely to be read during a security review.\n\nThe substantive correction is why an internal host is refused. Utils.getHostName\nsaid the render request built from that host carries Basic credentials, so a\nprivate address had to be rejected to prevent SSRF. Nothing is fetched from that\nhost any more - rendering goes to the local GraphQL endpoint - so the host is\nonly ever the citation URL stored in CustomGPT. The guard still earns its place,\nfor a different reason: a citation nobody outside the network can open is worse\nthan no citation. Same for normalizeServerName, which repeated the credential\nrationale twice, including for its https default.\n\nAlso:\n\n- the class javadoc listed \"the Jahia rendering password and the server-cookie\n  value\" among the write-only secrets; neither exists. It names the CustomGPT\n  token and the Jahia API token.\n- isHttpsUrl claimed to gate the Jahia rendering URL. It never does - its only\n  caller is the CustomGPT apiBaseUrl check.\n- okhttp3.Credentials was imported by CustomGptIndexerNodeHandler and unused.\n  Java does not fail on an unused import, so it survived the removal of the\n  Basic-auth code it belonged to.\n\nThe log line now says \"Refusing to index\" rather than \"Refusing to render\" and\nstates the consequence, since skipping is no longer about rendering at all.\n\nThe two Basic-auth mentions left in JahiaRenderClient are deliberate: they\nrecord what this class replaced.\n\nNo behaviour change: comments, one dead import, one log string. 341 tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrHYTIACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kFzwf/R3D+qsrsGUB8PKiVvn68b2q4B5pbO2tgSRmlT4ZO/s8DB9BpuuVZPJrB\ni5sfBsokm4zeFhDSWNg/bFpZXUZrjyq8O6W3OVi1/14wPKk1VBOP8VrRYMs/8XcP\nj0IdBOmBUY89P3brwjJJz/rbrSa869It4W2MxrLgCAuPxGD3uKLYfq8d9A2FgJA0\nuUthtG2QoeUqclDqFEiJNmSYQja4hL8SXBVbCKs4LmHJaGrfS6kYyX9KU+FEtjVb\nCovn6T7pbZk6JPJ1GTo/h7gPkvAgwSqeBjnx/gswSUMfv1PyOhhJZc5DQINNncnI\nsYCNWJzMZ9plmdpePJ3sjdXF6O+BLA==\n=Q6P1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T12:13:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/f7a8eb2aea1894f0640afd8b8c176c9105cb3f19","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGY3YThlYjJhZWExODk0ZjA2NDBhZmQ4YjhjMTc2YzkxMDVjYjNmMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/c2aaffb0758dbe1e5f6e450757cfe01b0fa53ca0","sha":"c2aaffb0758dbe1e5f6e450757cfe01b