_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/c2aaffb0758dbe1e5f6e450757cfe01b0fa53ca0","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGMyYWFmZmIwNzU4ZGJlMWU1ZjZlNDUwNzU3Y2ZlMDFiMGZhNTNjYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961","sha":"632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/d8fbe868bd4b67cbd57fef4b2c9418e4c0bdeec3","sha":"d8fbe868bd4b67cbd57fef4b2c9418e4c0bdeec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/d8fbe868bd4b67cbd57fef4b2c9418e4c0bdeec3"}],"sha":"c2aaffb0758dbe1e5f6e450757cfe01b0fa53ca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/c2aaffb0758dbe1e5f6e450757cfe01b0fa53ca0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/d8fbe868bd4b67cbd57fef4b2c9418e4c0bdeec3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:44:42Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:44:42Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor: remove the server cookie settings\n\nThe three serverCookie properties pinned a request to one cluster node behind a\nload balancer. That mattered when the module fetched a page''s public .html URL\nthrough the proxy. Rendering now goes to Jahia''s own GraphQL endpoint, local by\ndefault and documented as such, so pinning a request to the node it already runs\non does nothing.\n\nThey were also actively dangerous. Two of the three were a trap:\n\n    domain=[]            -> IllegalArgumentException: unexpected domain:\n    domain=[example.com] -> OK: n=v; domain=example.com; path=/; secure; httponly\n\nMeasured on OkHttp 4.12.0. The CookieJar guard checked name and value, then\ncalled .domain() unconditionally, and the shipped .cfg defaulted the domain to\nempty. So setting a name and a value - the obvious thing to do, the domain\nlooking optional - threw on every request from inside loadForRequest, stopping\nrendering with an error nowhere near the setting that caused it.\n\nAnd the Cookie header in JahiaRenderClient was dead code regardless. OkHttp''s\nBridgeInterceptor calls Request.Builder.header(\"Cookie\", ...) after\ncookieJar.loadForRequest, which replaces rather than appends; both paths were\ngated on the same two properties, so the jar always won.\n\nRemoved: the properties, their Config fields and accessors, the CookieJar and\nits okhttp3 imports, the header block, the GraphQL schema fields and mutation\narguments, the three admin inputs, every label in both resource bundles, and\nthe 4 e2e tests that covered them (spec 01: 29 -> 25).\n\nAGENTS.md listed jahiaServerCookieValue among the write-only secrets alongside\njahiaPassword, neither of which exists now; it names token and jahiaApiToken.\n\nThe redirect comment on jahiaClient still said the session cookie must not be\nforwarded. It is the API token that must not be.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c0ea5277ef67fe49faa9b4a4f87629c11698ce03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/c0ea5277ef67fe49faa9b4a4f87629c11698ce03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/d8fbe868bd4b67cbd57fef4b2c9418e4c0bdeec3","verification":{"payload":"tree c0ea5277ef67fe49faa9b4a4f87629c11698ce03\nparent 632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791449082 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791449082 +0200\n\nrefactor: remove the server cookie settings\n\nThe three serverCookie properties pinned a request to one cluster node behind a\nload balancer. That mattered when the module fetched a page''s public .html URL\nthrough the proxy. Rendering now goes to Jahia''s own GraphQL endpoint, local by\ndefault and documented as such, so pinning a request to the node it already runs\non does nothing.\n\nThey were also actively dangerous. Two of the three were a trap:\n\n    domain=[]            -> IllegalArgumentException: unexpected domain:\n    domain=[example.com] -> OK: n=v; domain=example.com; path=/; secure; httponly\n\nMeasured on OkHttp 4.12.0. The CookieJar guard checked name and value, then\ncalled .domain() unconditionally, and the shipped .cfg defaulted the domain to\nempty. So setting a name and a value - the obvious thing to do, the domain\nlooking optional - threw on every request from inside loadForRequest, stopping\nrendering with an error nowhere near the setting that caused it.\n\nAnd the Cookie header in JahiaRenderClient was dead code regardless. OkHttp''s\nBridgeInterceptor calls Request.Builder.header(\"Cookie\", ...) after\ncookieJar.loadForRequest, which replaces rather than appends; both paths were\ngated on the same two properties, so the jar always won.\n\nRemoved: the properties, their Config fields and accessors, the CookieJar and\nits okhttp3 imports, the header block, the GraphQL schema fields and mutation\narguments, the three admin inputs, every label in both resource bundles, and\nthe 4 e2e tests that covered them (spec 01: 29 -> 25).\n\nAGENTS.md listed jahiaServerCookieValue among the write-only secrets alongside\njahiaPassword, neither of which exists now; it names token and jahiaApiToken.\n\nThe redirect comment on jahiaClient still said the session cookie must not be\nforwarded. It is the API token that must not be.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrHV/oACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mX2Af/bUR0SPsQAwGZd/u7eFLol7FEcDs7j129Wgje/FWfmI0xmHUHERekjVan\n2aET3of7PPp7rn8TT5jX3PaXjLW5wYHGpPCaaCpvIASlhjUdG9buVcsQAiDv9nma\nlYwpwTi3uMX5sld7PysQQCyRgB98oQSQi6OinPAzfmzjpeU5Dtny38JbqiI02V1V\nhLNhw6DvhJkoysdHqCOs+AAzCwf5a4zCf+v4od7SGmPQnp6aopRGnVBlMz6vr7/P\n1Y7yRjlxLnV0oYjH5ppYE6aLbviJo8MgtppGrNzSrG+EN+apXNEksDT0MhkCHWWl\nWZUUjgFALgz9s5Qwvg6Q5uWY2gMr4A==\n=tUc4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:54:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbour