"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDYzMjQyN2EyZDE4MGVmNjIyYjE3M2E5YTIwYjBhZDMyNzUxZjY5NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/7bac965a0a9f3f5d7b762e16840fef126924b8e4","sha":"7bac965a0a9f3f5d7b762e16840fef126924b8e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/7bac965a0a9f3f5d7b762e16840fef126924b8e4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/a81e3bada44aea27de11727427405377592e6716","sha":"a81e3bada44aea27de11727427405377592e6716","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/a81e3bada44aea27de11727427405377592e6716"}],"sha":"632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/632427a2d180ef622b173a9a20b0ad32751f6961"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/a81e3bada44aea27de11727427405377592e6716/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:05:57Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:05:57Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor: drop the stale credential getter names from GqlSettings\n\nRemoving Basic authentication repointed two accessors at the new fields but\nleft their old names in place, so main carried:\n\n    @GraphQLName(\"jahiaGraphqlEndpoint\")\n    public String getJahiaPassword() {\n        return jahiaGraphqlEndpoint;\n    }\n\nThe schema was always correct - graphql-java names a field from @GraphQLName,\nnot from the method - which is why every test stayed green. The cost was in\nreading it: an accessor whose name promises a secret and returns a URL stops a\nsecurity review dead, and invites the next refactor to \"fix\" it the wrong way.\n\nRenamed to getJahiaApiToken() and getJahiaGraphqlEndpoint(), matching every\nother getter in the class. No schema change, no behaviour change.\n\nAlso drops what the same removal left behind:\n\n- label.jahiaUsername / label.jahiaPassword in the de/en/fr bundles. Dead - the\n  React panel reads javascript/locales/*.json, and all 56 keys it asks for\n  resolve there.\n- KEY_USERNAME / KEY_PASSWORD in ConfigParseTest, which seeded two keys Config\n  no longer knows, documenting a config shape that no longer exists.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a19c6f5752adcb776c4d9b4c7d8808c830dfb17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/5a19c6f5752adcb776c4d9b4c7d8808c830dfb17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/a81e3bada44aea27de11727427405377592e6716","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a19c6f5752adcb776c4d9b4c7d8808c830dfb17\nparent 7bac965a0a9f3f5d7b762e16840fef126924b8e4\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791446757 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791446757 +0200\n\nrefactor: drop the stale credential getter names from GqlSettings\n\nRemoving Basic authentication repointed two accessors at the new fields but\nleft their old names in place, so main carried:\n\n    @GraphQLName(\"jahiaGraphqlEndpoint\")\n    public String getJahiaPassword() {\n        return jahiaGraphqlEndpoint;\n    }\n\nThe schema was always correct - graphql-java names a field from @GraphQLName,\nnot from the method - which is why every test stayed green. The cost was in\nreading it: an accessor whose name promises a secret and returns a URL stops a\nsecurity review dead, and invites the next refactor to \"fix\" it the wrong way.\n\nRenamed to getJahiaApiToken() and getJahiaGraphqlEndpoint(), matching every\nother getter in the class. No schema change, no behaviour change.\n\nAlso drops what the same removal left behind:\n\n- label.jahiaUsername / label.jahiaPassword in the de/en/fr bundles. Dead - the\n  React panel reads javascript/locales/*.json, and all 56 keys it asks for\n  resolve there.\n- KEY_USERNAME / KEY_PASSWORD in ConfigParseTest, which seeded two keys Config\n  no longer knows, docum