/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/ec4c90e2d27ad7c0c61ed5616e802dd0da398a2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T20:14:06Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T20:14:06Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"docs: document rendering through GraphQL with a read-only indexer\n\nReplaces the retired credential pair in the settings table and adds a\nsection on what actually matters when configuring this: the endpoint\nis local by design, the account doing the rendering decides what lands\nin the corpus, and the indexer is not supposed to see everything.\n\nThe three-row table is the part worth keeping. Rendering as an\nadministrator puts Preview, Page Composer and Logout into the indexed\ncontent; rendering as nobody puts the login form there instead. Both\nwere measured on the Digitall home page rather than assumed, and they\ndiffer by exactly those words.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d24c310d81169e806f3a9d41c7fce00e7552a928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/d24c310d81169e806f3a9d41c7fce00e7552a928"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/ec4c90e2d27ad7c0c61ed5616e802dd0da398a2a","verification":{"payload":"tree d24c310d81169e806f3a9d41c7fce00e7552a928\nparent 87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791404046 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791404046 +0200\n\ndocs: document rendering through GraphQL with a read-only indexer\n\nReplaces the retired credential pair in the settings table and adds a\nsection on what actually matters when configuring this: the endpoint\nis local by design, the account doing the rendering decides what lands\nin the corpus, and the indexer is not supposed to see everything.\n\nThe three-row table is the part worth keeping. Rendering as an\nadministrator puts Preview, Page Composer and Logout into the indexed\ncontent; rendering as nobody puts the login form there instead. Both\nwere measured on the Digitall home page rather than assumed, and they\ndiffer by exactly those words.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrGqA4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nutAf/csS+F1LtvXpL8UxycXAN+Lc53wr79GrOK8GLLbsNGzbThfDITZpbwjY9\nGZfiQRt+TqXuSzO7488veYgAjK7Xqu1ZyGZEWRDxk7pNbFTnhScS4u/6Ntb4gYP+\nGSjY2gcMJRr/MFVwtePhtIhK/7153ALwhKSgLRQ1pI/YbjFwfaKZVLSqgOfp1ZiY\nAMFHRbNJ0J2Yx8C3QSYfMLrNju2yFoCyiOFzt4J7eJ4lhEz+06fv4UzmOuBriOpG\njtCiq6CXN1dOEIzJd4pJ8qBkzNp4KnBBP96HN4eLCMiKojO0ltYxP6dYZ3cDplac\ne+oD71JHc10eCNukTw7v9+mk4KcMvA==\n=pNxd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T20:29:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/ec4c90e2d27ad7c0c61ed5616e802dd0da398a2a","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGVjNGM5MGUyZDI3YWQ3YzBjNjFlZDU2MTZlODAyZGQwZGEzOThhMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5","sha":"87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5"}],"sha":"ec4c90e2d27ad7c0c61ed5616e802dd0da398a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/ec4c90e2d27ad7c0c61ed5616e802dd0da398a2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T20:04:39Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T20:04:39Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: render content nodes as modules, not as pages\n\nThe module indexes jnt:page AND jmix:mainResource content, and the\nGraphQL render asked for a page configuration for both. A content node\nhas no page template, so Jahia answered TemplateNotFoundException and\nthe node failed - /sites/digitall/contents/person-portrait-1 is the\none in the harness. A page keeps the full-document configuration; any\nother node is rendered on its own.\n\nThat is also the better content to index: a module render carries none\nof the page furniture, which is the same reason the indexing account\nis a read-only one rather than root.\n\nHarness: the Jahia image bundles personal-api-tokens 1.9.0, which\nstarts cleanly, logs nothing wrong, registers 22 views - and never\ncontributes admin.personalApiTokens to the GraphQL schema. Minting a\ntoken then fails as a VALIDATION error, reading like a bad query\nrather than a missing capability. 1.10.0 is installed explicitly with\nuninstallPreviousVersion so the bundled copy cannot win.\n\nSpecs now provision a dedicated read-only customgpt-indexer account\nand mint its own token: personal tokens belong to the calling user, so\nthere is no minting one on somebody else''s behalf. The configuration\nis built inside the callback that produces the token, because Cypress\nqueues commands up front and a token read from an outer variable is\nstill empty when the saveSettings command is queued.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ffa4ba3dc0973186bd62ebe4c7d57c3b1d604b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/0ffa4ba3dc0973186bd62ebe4c7d57c3b1d604b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ffa4ba3dc0973186bd62ebe4c7d57c3b1d604b8\nparent b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791403479 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791403479 +0200\n\nfix: render content nodes as modules, not as pages\n\nThe module indexes jnt:page AND jmix:mainResource content, and the\nGraphQL render asked for a page configuration for both. A content node\nhas no page template, so Jahia answered TemplateNotFoundException and\nthe node failed - /sites/digitall/contents/person-portrait-1 is the\none in the harness. A page keeps the full-document configuration; any\nother node is rendered on its own.\n\nThat is also the better content to index: a module render carries none\nof the page furniture, which is the same reason the indexing account\nis a read-only one rather than root.\n\nHarness: the Jahia image bundles personal-api-tokens 1.9.0, which\nstarts cleanly, logs nothing wrong, registers 22 views - and never\ncontributes admin.personalApiTokens to the GraphQL schema. Minting a\ntoken then fails as a VALIDATION error, reading like a bad query\nrather than a missing capability. 1.10.0 is installed explicitly with\nuninstallPreviousVersion so the bundled copy cannot win.\n\nSpecs now provision a dedicated read-only customgpt-indexer account\nand mint its own token: personal tokens belong to the calling user, so\nthere is no minting one on somebody else''s behalf. The configuration\nis built inside the callback that produces the token, because Cypress\nqueues commands up front and a token read from an outer variable is\nstill empty when the saveSettings command is queued.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrGpdcACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nifQf/Vz5/eWInlN8FApjLi13E06cQ9ZSsmHL54tXs87mQW1viyXidu0NWuy2J\nAlgRlCiFbuu4Eelzxc80wlcojqq5X3vmzIY8nYKKgvM0NBLtKgxcY0KT8IuN6acj\nqd9fU6HCkspjgBwJTTimMUDsIqL0CxnSmdHxLZJwC9Ppc65PcUE1PSiJgb5RuGPT\nfLAxcV+38bg1iK04FRQ5Qk5/TJP0kYhn+lfq5+LodrCvVBdbnXg23hpt9RxPBd8M\nBr2UceSTdrjZoMFI+xMKSdUoWJh7gE3+UQ+DY2bRos/MHStsZ2xLm0xX/CbUYWHr\nsfR2MqFc2b/waCuWe/egUbEJsETSqg==\n=GJnJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T20:29:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDg3Y2Q5MDExYjQzZDI2ZGUyNjJhMGVkZjE3YjI5M2Y0NGVkMzVkYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914","sha":"b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914"}],"sha":"87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/87cd9011b43d26de262a0edf17b293f44ed35dc5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:27:22Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:27:22Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat: render pages through GraphQL with a personal API token\n\nBasic authentication is blocked in some environments, so the module\ncan no longer reach restricted pages by fetching their public URL with\na username and password. Pages are now rendered through Jahia''s own\nGraphQL endpoint, authenticated with a personal API token.\n\nRendering in-process was the obvious alternative and does not work:\nJahia executes JSP views by dispatching through the servlet container,\nso RenderService outside a real request has no RequestDispatcher. The\nGraphQL servlet has one, which is what makes this approach work at all\n- the container is borrowed rather than avoided.\n\nThree gains beyond unblocking:\n\nNo password travels anywhere. A token is scoped to graphql, revocable\non its own, and minted for a dedicated read-only account rather than\nfor root.\n\nThe call goes to a LOCAL endpoint, decoupling the fetch target from\nthe citation URL. They were the same value before, so a fetch went\nback out through the proxy and bot protection in front of the public\nhost - which is why fetching needed a configurable user agent and\nsame-origin redirect handling at all.\n\nContent the indexing account cannot read now comes back as a\nstructured access denial with a null node, so it is skipped rather\nthan indexed. Fetching it over HTTP as an unauthorised user answered\n200 with a login form, and \"Username\", \"Password\", \"Remember Me\" went\ninto the corpus as page content. A skip is logged at INFO and is NOT a\nfailure: the account is deliberately restricted, so treating it as one\nwould mark every site FAILED on every run.\n\nFiles no longer travel over HTTP at all - their bytes are read\nstraight from the repository, which is where they already were.\n\njahiaUsername and jahiaPassword are gone rather than deprecated, along\nwith the HTTP fetch path they existed for: buildRenderRequest, the\nsame-origin redirect follower and their tests. The render tests they\ncovered are replaced by tests on the new envelope handling, which keep\nthe distinction those encoded - a failure must be raised, never\nsilently skipped.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4dc050e708c02b4cf1bd0d63888da09e0094ea3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/4dc050e708c02b4cf1bd0d63888da09e0094ea3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dc050e708c02b4cf1bd0d63888da09e0094ea3f\nparent 6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791401242 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791401242 +0200\n\nfeat: render pages through GraphQL with a personal API token\n\nBasic authentication is blocked in some environments, so the module\ncan no longer reach restricted pages by fetching their public URL with\na username and password. Pages are now rendered through Jahia''s own\nGraphQL endpoint, authenticated with a personal API token.\n\nRendering in-process was the obvious alternative and does not work:\nJahia executes JSP views by dispatching through the servlet container,\nso RenderService outside a real request has no RequestDispatcher. The\nGraphQL servlet has one, which is what makes this approach work at all\n- the container is borrowed rather than avoided.\n\nThree gains beyond unblocking:\n\nNo password travels anywhere. A token is scoped to graphql, revocable\non its own, and minted for a dedicated read-only account rather than\nfor root.\n\nThe call goes to a LOCAL endpoint, decoupling the fetch target from\nthe citation URL. They were the same value before, so a fetch went\nback out through the proxy and bot protection in front of the public\nhost - which is why fetching needed a configurable user agent and\nsame-origin redirect handling at all.\n\nContent the indexing account cannot read now comes back as a\nstructured access denial with a null node, so it is skipped rather\nthan indexed. Fetching it over HTTP as an unauthorised user answered\n200 with a login form, and \"Username\", \"Password\", \"Remember Me\" went\ninto the corpus as page content. A skip is logged at INFO and is NOT a\nfailure: the account is deliberately restricted, so treating it as one\nwould mark every site FAILED on every run.\n\nFiles no longer travel over HTTP at all - their bytes are read\nstraight from the repository, which is where they already were.\n\njahiaUsername and jahiaPassword are gone rather than deprecated, along\nwith the HTTP fetch path they existed for: buildRenderRequest, the\nsame-origin redirect follower and their tests. The render tests they\ncovered are replaced by tests on the new envelope handling, which keep\nthe distinction those encoded - a failure must be raised, never\nsilently skipped.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrGnRoACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kC/Af/WBTqt3Sv/x8+4eGcwA/HpLZydM0ms/Q8k2pCCHNOIP5sxTcQ39qaTu0B\nh5ws7Wh6Qe4JjCi0TyZLTVlWUxjPOe2eJ34B3pFADsKAhwJCl05X/4ZuvI/34tBP\nMuxbM4WHNhDv8VGUKnsUhnF5szBQcCwhMhGVWqwzx/j84rpLq5rg1rSgL9Pn4wNQ\nWmtHKWUMu/+Pu3o50EQxGNQBtRRg88cnBNmtoV9Utndx2o6Xe27UOcF4Fr1Gnbmg\nV9LD3OIKqqyCGAPy3urUvuJIyrN4v9xvBhbE7nur4SPiOtj/eDvRLjaD9Ux1JDzJ\nGk6D5mw9lBkdi5rXHkILj16ZDExQow==\n=uVVU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T20:29:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGI5OTQxNzQ2ODhmMzFiOWU3NzQ0NTcyNjQ4OGYxZjE4NDExY2I5MTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f","sha":"6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f"}],"sha":"b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/b994174688f31b9e77445726488f1f18411cb914"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:38:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:38:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: stop the server-name spec racing the coalescing window\n\nThe override test issued its index request once, right after the\nbefore hook published the page. Publishing queues an index of its own,\nand the module holds a node''s coalescing key until that indexation''s\nFUTURE completes - later than the page id appearing. The log shows the\nrequest arriving 261ms after the page id was written and being dropped\nanyway: \"Coalesced 1 index operation(s); 0 operation(s) dispatched\".\nThe page kept the URL the publication run gave it and the assertion\nwaited two minutes for a host that was never coming.\n\nNothing to do with the binary-upload change on this branch: pages take\nthe same path through it as before. It is the same coalescing\nmechanism that made the two tests collide earlier, reached this time\nthrough the publication rather than a sibling test.\n\nThere is no external signal for that window, so the test no longer\ntries to time it - it re-issues the request on every poll attempt\nuntil one dispatches. The README now says the window lasts until the\nindexation completes, rather than implying it is only about two\nrequests sent close together.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c881d53d9e71abf38baea9d18b9be8d4a2803c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/1c881d53d9e71abf38baea9d18b9be8d4a2803c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c881d53d9e71abf38baea9d18b9be8d4a2803c7\nparent f7a77e6fd88557278b223f68c5f487006784dff3\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791398330 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791398330 +0200\n\ntest: stop the server-name spec racing the coalescing window\n\nThe override test issued its index request once, right after the\nbefore hook published the page. Publishing queues an index of its own,\nand the module holds a node''s coalescing key until that indexation''s\nFUTURE completes - later than the page id appearing. The log shows the\nrequest arriving 261ms after the page id was written and being dropped\nanyway: \"Coalesced 1 index operation(s); 0 operation(s) dispatched\".\nThe page kept the URL the publication run gave it and the assertion\nwaited two minutes for a host that was never coming.\n\nNothing to do with the binary-upload change on this branch: pages take\nthe same path through it as before. It is the same coalescing\nmechanism that made the two tests collide earlier, reached this time\nthrough the publication rather than a sibling test.\n\nThere is no external signal for that window, so the test no longer\ntries to time it - it re-issues the request on every poll attempt\nuntil one dispatches. The README now says the window lasts until the\nindexation completes, rather than implying it is only about two\nrequests sent close together.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrGkboACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mGuQgAhnlTW3aBsH+udjU1+6ge8E77GpAsSZoIp81AJHCOOLYFWIpp7OhalzQU\npKAqaTyuNbdJKZzh4KdDKUWBPkcScX3qENFWDWyrrJa/9mEYoHxS4Sm9bkpvMaSr\nA4oO3lcHJAp44cL1kgOKWe/RKnKFlowZXOyXflkS5LFzgQ2F3WUEB/JyohVoiA+q\nxFWmmF3ccWpWzDFZJ+9OEbTJYqbhl2ndYyX6uXrsEHzEtmsqO+QCwCTNx+Y3OL7w\nLdBrqQYCthe5fGQ2CWPkR9Kj4qHi2kvf4lRXFV8+ayaZ+wmV0PMhcasdd0VHuQaz\n4zWgIuNLxaqoRK/LN9akHD2ldomQRw==\n=caFs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:02:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDYwMDdiYmNhZGE0N2EwMjg2NDdmYzhkN2QwYzJmNjA3YWY4ZDAxOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/f7a77e6fd88557278b223f68c5f487006784dff3","sha":"f7a77e6fd88557278b223f68c5f487006784dff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/f7a77e6fd88557278b223f68c5f487006784dff3"}],"sha":"6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/6007bbcada47a028647fc8d7d0c2f607af8d019f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/f7a77e6fd88557278b223f68c5f487006784dff3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:25:09Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:25:09Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: upload files as bytes, not as a UTF-8 round-trip of their content\n\nFiles and rendered pages share one indexing path, and that path read\nevery response body with body().string() and uploaded\noutput.getBytes(UTF_8) announced as text/html. For a binary that is a\ndecode-and-re-encode: every byte sequence that is not valid UTF-8\nbecomes U+FFFD.\n\nMeasured on the Digitall sample rather than reasoned about. The\n155,468-byte PDF came back out at 264,461 bytes with 154,804 of its\nbytes changed - only the %PDF- header survived. The upload returned\n2xx every time, so nothing ever reported it, and no PDF in any project\nhas held its real content.\n\nA file is now read with body().bytes() and announced with the type\nJahia served it as, falling back to the node''s own jcr:mimeType and\nthen to application/octet-stream. Rendered pages are unchanged.\n\nThe multipart file name for a file is now the node name rather than\nthe display title. The title carries no extension - \"Digitall\nFinancial Report\" tells CustomGPT nothing about what it has been\nhanded when the content type is generic.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"64d86608d80892df48adb4831c5e3b0211b24ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/64d86608d80892df48adb4831c5e3b0211b24ba9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/f7a77e6fd88557278b223f68c5f487006784dff3","verification":{"payload":"tree 64d86608d80892df48adb4831c5e3b0211b24ba9\nparent 8141942d8c5c4d44cb1d6bc54ca5d4d2b61240d2\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791397509 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791397509 +0200\n\nfix: upload files as bytes, not as a UTF-8 round-trip of their content\n\nFiles and rendered pages share one indexing path, and that path read\nevery response body with body().string() and uploaded\noutput.getBytes(UTF_8) announced as text/html. For a binary that is a\ndecode-and-re-encode: every byte sequence that is not valid UTF-8\nbecomes U+FFFD.\n\nMeasured on the Digitall sample rather than reasoned about. The\n155,468-byte PDF came back out at 264,461 bytes with 154,804 of its\nbytes changed - only the %PDF- header survived. The upload returned\n2xx every time, so nothing ever reported it, and no PDF in any project\nhas held its real content.\n\nA file is now read with body().bytes() and announced with the type\nJahia served it as, falling back to the node''s own jcr:mimeType and\nthen to application/octet-stream. Rendered pages are unchanged.\n\nThe multipart file name for a file is now the node name rather than\nthe display title. The title carries no extension - \"Digitall\nFinancial Report\" tells CustomGPT nothing about what it has been\nhanded when the content type is generic.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrGjoUACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3luQwf9FqqBYyOToaNSDXwXQ3aYYe1rWUL6ziw32AYIEuA06TAG/p4zICgXUmZg\n2nRuI+aEwG6/e+irqw7FzsS207Er7kIjnGJFVN+fga8csW7ITobP80Fcd82PXCHL\nHmvemNVFQTJwUUAFIVI7Wqmmqs2LLApoG8dGFoe0o1500EXELYvyDTFYIl8l1oJu\nNWwMU9+/RBQLg+Mb39cvJkVAbCnuNo0f7YD6UpFPpG4Xed83POZAFnpWeO+Vvm5B\nGpSyFSWKig5FrVDZ+/7UbVQP4+uOeXB8KlZ3DQ8N37ZwQ+r5yg8K3Me0clrTZbeS\npXu5bJnx4AlJRKmFjgY00GFNSMyCrw==\n=ks9z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:02:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co