l":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/eb86185af0ec7c9f7a71ee257bd9d068b0aff328","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGViODYxODVhZjBlYzdjOWY3YTcxZWUyNTdiZDlkMDY4YjBhZmYzMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f","sha":"82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6","sha":"f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6"}],"sha":"eb86185af0ec7c9f7a71ee257bd9d068b0aff328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/eb86185af0ec7c9f7a71ee257bd9d068b0aff328"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:32:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:32:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat(service): resolve the SGE deployment, and close it when the quota is spent\n\nThe Academy search page offers CustomGPT''s Search Generative Experience when\nAugmented Search finds nothing. Two things it needs were being supplied by\nhand: the project id and the public deployment key, typed into component\nproperties by an editor. That is a credential hazard rather than a chore. The\nfield sits next to a project id in an editor form and the obvious wrong thing\nto paste into it is this module''s API token, which is a real secret and would\nland in page source.\n\nBoth are already derivable here. The project id is in configuration, and the\npublic key is the shareable_slug field of the GET /projects/{id} payload this\nmodule already reads the project name from. getSgeDeployment() returns the\ntwo of them together with an availability flag, in a type that deliberately\nhas no way to carry the token.\n\nAvailability answers the other question: whether the team still has query\nquota. GET /limits/usage reports max_queries for the billing cycle against\ncurrent_queries, so \"the quota is spent\" is a read rather than an inference,\nand a spent quota now hides the button instead of letting a visitor click into\nCustomGPT''s own error.\n\nCached for five minutes, because without a cache every render of a search page\nwould make two authenticated calls, one of them to an endpoint that is itself\nrate limited: page views would turn into API spend and then into 429s. Quota\nmoves slowly, so the cost of being up to five minutes stale is a handful of\nvisitors at the boundary. The cache is dropped when the configuration changes,\nor a new project id would appear not to have taken effect for five minutes.\n\nFails open throughout. Availability goes false only when the quota is\npositively known to be spent; a timeout, a 429, a missing field or a\nnon-positive max_queries (how an unmetered plan reads) all leave the feature\non. Hiding a working feature on a transient error is the worse failure: the\nvisitor loses a route that would have worked and nothing says why, whereas\nletting one doomed query through costs a visible error message they can act\non.\n\nThe quota decision is split from the request so it is testable without a\nnetwork: 15 new tests, most of them pinning the fail-open cases, plus one\nasserting the key never reaches toString(). 259 tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"89f57277d2ca2c953bfd93c1cc2d3455da0a261a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/89f57277d2ca2c953bfd93c1cc2d3455da0a261a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6","verification":{"payload":"tree 89f57277d2ca2c953bfd93c1cc2d3455da0a261a\nparent 82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791005554 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1791005554 +0200\n\nfeat(service): resolve the SGE deployment, and close it when the quota is spent\n\nThe Academy search page offers CustomGPT''s Search Generative Experience when\nAugmented Search finds nothing. Two things it needs were being supplied by\nhand: the project id and the public deployment key, typed into component\nproperties by an editor. That is a credential hazard rather than a chore. The\nfield sits next to a project id in an editor form and the obvious wrong thing\nto paste into it is this module''s API token, which is a real secret and would\nland in page source.\n\nBoth are already derivable here. The project id is in configuration, and the\npublic key is the shareable_slug field of the GET /projects/{id} payload this\nmodule already reads the project name from. getSgeDeployment() returns the\ntwo of them together with an availability flag, in a type that deliberately\nhas no way to carry the token.\n\nAvailability answers the other question: whether the team still has query\nquota. GET /limits/usage reports max_queries for the billing cycle against\ncurrent_queries, so \"the quota is spent\" is a read rather than an inference,\nand a spent quota now hides the button instead of letting a visitor click into\nCustomGPT''s own error.\n\nCached for five minutes, because without a cache every render of a search page\nwould make two authenticated calls, one of them to an endpoint that is itself\nrate limited: page views would turn into API spend and then into 429s. Quota\nmoves slowly, so the cost of being up to five minutes stale is a handful of\nvisitors at the boundary. The cache is dropped when the configuration changes,\nor a new project id would appear not to have taken effect for five minutes.\n\nFails open throughout. Availability goes false only when the quota is\npositively known to be spent; a timeout, a 429, a missing field or a\nnon-positive max_queries (how an unmetered plan reads) all leave the feature\non. Hiding a working feature on a transient error is the worse failure: the\nvisitor loses a route that would have worked and nothing says why, whereas\nletting one doomed query through costs a visible error message they can act\non.\n\nThe quota decision is split from the request so it is testable without a\nnetwork: 15 new tests, most of them pinning the fail-open cases, plus one\nasserting the key never reaches toString(). 259 tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAk3IACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mh5wgAtvV9RQljqSFjO/VF+4kghLSw8o9ylxqCIx5i1ol9cYBFYGv0UORWonRb\n9/VcXJM+EkDJ/lWnXmxtET53RYv3Bk9zvggW5V0JmabZ/A+/PywgPhpOFMRThBWa\n6NYDxNNlGYPy/ckYbwBvQ3VW60XEePMwAAi6Shzlt8KoKLqWHJNVjpTilGaP8CU1\naPcy2t9sFaPGf5/on63OBx9khi27iuOtibCJzREafp0lY5FhdSJJkNd+wPbrC1Vn\nSgt5Mh92r1o+zD2dyON8cmugIFs4o05bkeT61OTcd9OSYEOH6La9xWfPCcp0DzIq\neqXKWWpUeJ53kGpXx9jVEHzMmVXyDQ==\n=YW2/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T05:32:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGY1YTJkYzUwN2IyNDAzNTlkYTgzNDEzNjVhMDA2NWE3MTAyNzA3YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f","sha":"82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f"}],"sha":"f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/f5a2dc507b240359da8341365a0065a7102707b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/4c02d3c12479335794bc75a62fdc54de18bddb71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:43:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:37:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat(scripts): also retire the Jahia 8.1 documentation\n\nAdds documentation/jahia/8_1 (199 jnt:page) to the roots and allows it through\nthe documentation/jahia rule, which keeps 8_2 and any future version protected.\n\nThis root is different in kind from the other two, and the comment on it says\nso. The archives were deleted from CustomGPT in September, so every DELETE this\nscript queues for them is a no-op against an id that is already gone. The 8.1\npages are still in the live corpus, so marking them actively removes them and\nthe chatbot stops being able to answer about 8.1 at all. That is a decision\nabout who the chatbot serves rather than cleanup, so the line is written to be\ncommented out on its own if the archives should go first.\n\nThe dry run now reports per root as well as in total: the roots differ in\nconsequence, so one aggregate number should not be the only number on screen\nbefore DRY_RUN is turned off.\n\nThe allowed-version list in the guard and the jahia/* entries in ROOTS are kept\nas two separate lists on purpose, so a typo in one cannot quietly disarm the\nother. The guard test asserts 8_2 is still protected after the change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cdd9004fcef592e32642cd7291b4bba3f345e3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/1cdd9004fcef592e32642cd7291b4bba3f345e3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/4c02d3c12479335794bc75a62fdc54de18bddb71","verification":{"payload":"tree 1cdd9004fcef592e32642cd7291b4bba3f345e3d\nparent b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790970211 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790973443 +0200\n\nfeat(scripts): also retire the Jahia 8.1 documentation\n\nAdds documentation/jahia/8_1 (199 jnt:page) to the roots and allows it through\nthe documentation/jahia rule, which keeps 8_2 and any future version protected.\n\nThis root is different in kind from the other two, and the comment on it says\nso. The archives were deleted from CustomGPT in September, so every DELETE this\nscript queues for them is a no-op against an id that is already gone. The 8.1\npages are still in the live corpus, so marking them actively removes them and\nthe chatbot stops being able to answer about 8.1 at all. That is a decision\nabout who the chatbot serves rather than cleanup, so the line is written to be\ncommented out on its own if the archives should go first.\n\nThe dry run now reports per root as well as in total: the roots differ in\nconsequence, so one aggregate number should not be the only number on screen\nbefore DRY_RUN is turned off.\n\nThe allowed-version list in the guard and the jahia/* entries in ROOTS are kept\nas two separate lists on purpose, so a typo in one cannot quietly disarm the\nother. The guard test asserts 8_2 is still protected after the change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAFgMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n3JAf/TW1In8hWoXuQ/gOd3g+x0/bzIf2mM1g7KFop4DyaiywntXks0JRRxvAQ\nhPPxhEWmU/T28A8vPR0hxA/vIPc/qX7W5njQQ5Rf91d2qoVUsNrOLjELd8/6NKgD\nDPGdlHxwE/bMuhyiEZ0ZHZHxchuVwTwLoanSC1bla1BI6FoTk54JmoUH6/W+bRcA\nxmimUTjRjXeJVJhujGCxe88AnItDtOyi/YozY2Eaty1GPTcp5aqLe3AxsdZEv/nc\nBL7fsepNL7BL0SW47cdAzjPpE0op6Hd9DkD5ysUc9a1a3YQt1gspzSu+gcUTWqvM\nZkLyU3or1n3TP4KR9sJCG/dtCEwTIQ==\n=mJ5z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/4c02d3c12479335794bc75a62fdc54de18bddb71","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDRjMDJkM2MxMjQ3OTMzNTc5NGJjNzVhNjJmZGM1NGRlMThiZGRiNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435","sha":"b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435"}],"sha":"4c02d3c12479335794bc75a62fdc54de18bddb71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/4c02d3c12479335794bc75a62fdc54de18bddb71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:40:42Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:37:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(scripts): match protected trees by prefix, not by substring\n\nThe guard flagged 18 archived pages as protected and aborted the run. They are\nlegacy-1/1/sysadmin/release-notes/jexperience-1.11.x -- jExperience 1.11\nrelease notes, archived content that is exactly what this script should mark --\ncaught by a bare \"jexperience\" substring test.\n\nWhat makes a page current is where its tree starts, not a product name\nappearing somewhere along its path. Protection is now a list of whole-path\nprefixes matched at a segment boundary, plus one rule for everything under\ndocumentation/jahia that is not the 7_3 archive, so 8_1, 8_2 and any version\ndirectory added later are covered without touching this list again.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 3.0.8; the guard, regenerated from the script''s own\ndefinitions, passes 10 archived paths including three of the 18 that failed,\naborts on 10 current ones including a hypothetical 9_0, and both roots stay\nclean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"20aae54802af0896cd3d3d846e25455e6f844cbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/20aae54802af0896cd3d3d846e25455e6f844cbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435","verification":{"payload":"tree 20aae54802af0896cd3d3d846e25455e6f844cbf\nparent 71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790970042 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790973443 +0200\n\nfix(scripts): match protected trees by prefix, not by substring\n\nThe guard flagged 18 archived pages as protected and aborted the run. They are\nlegacy-1/1/sysadmin/release-notes/jexperience-1.11.x -- jExperience 1.11\nrelease notes, archived content that is exactly what this script should mark --\ncaught by a bare \"jexperience\" substring test.\n\nWhat makes a page current is where its tree starts, not a product name\nappearing somewhere along its path. Protection is now a list of whole-path\nprefixes matched at a segment boundary, plus one rule for everything under\ndocumentation/jahia that is not the 7_3 archive, so 8_1, 8_2 and any version\ndirectory added later are covered without touching this list again.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 3.0.8; the guard, regenerated from the script''s own\ndefinitions, passes 10 archived paths including three of the 18 that failed,\naborts on 10 current ones including a hypothetical 9_0, and both roots stay\nclean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAFgMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3m8YQgAzlaatqBxRRK9c1AXfMm1Nw88BBN9BGIzGO8y8nwTmIuzwQ2cr3tlNaUX\nyPujf+K0ivA6LBGG8s3WiQ8DUYUTDCQY0R0pUwu9GCTKrCHF8vCbrjMLTgtS4J6e\nowQsL6TSQNIVL9oOd511xBlM7+1UbuvcaN59rxgpv/s7EOkfljSFOL2vnO2kWZjl\npzSbxZ1O3d1ucVwqt/1VHZ6o038ROMxwYiClJVzrVBlL7AsQykurEqMPc4g1Ep0C\n4FGP+B456rt2qj3BtUppHJzjc3mpeSuDQNviWwM0teDI6W9SjzqEkheVT+VDc4Lg\nrGYEBCjutbrcZ/0QcjWeipwbx65JZg==\n=Cb/t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGI2OTI3MTI3Yzk3ZmFjY2UzNGI5NDM1MzljMTU1NTg2ZDU5ODg0MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb","sha":"71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb"}],"sha":"b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/b6927127c97facce34b943539c155586d5988435"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:36:26Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:37:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(scripts): the 7.3 root is 7_3, not the export''s XML escaping\n\nSecond abort, and my mistake: I read _x0037__3 out of the export XML and took\nit for the JCR name. It is not. The exporter escapes any node name that is not\na legal XML element name, and an element name cannot start with a digit -- the\nrepository stores 7_3, with siblings 8_1 and 8_2. The home 404 page exporting\nas <_x0034_04> is the same escaping and confirms it.\n\nRoot is now documentation/jahia/7_3.\n\nSame correction in the guard, which matters more: the pattern added last commit\n(/_x003[89]__\\d) could never match a JCR path, so it protected nothing. Current\ndocs are documentation/jahia/8_1 and 8_2, now matched by /[89]_\\d. The dotted\njahia-8.x patterns are kept for titles and vanity URLs, where the dot is real.\n\nThe guard test now also asserts that the configured roots do not trip the guard\nthemselves, which is the check that would have caught this class of error\nwithout a round trip through the instance.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 3.0.8; guard passes 6 legacy paths, aborts on 9\ncurrent ones including bare 8_2, and both roots are clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7afb849684bbc0513ab6280ab67312991e74fed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/b7afb849684bbc0513ab6280ab67312991e74fed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb","verification":{"payload":"tree b7afb849684bbc0513ab6280ab67312991e74fed\nparent 2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790969786 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790973443 +0200\n\nfix(scripts): the 7.3 root is 7_3, not the export''s XML escaping\n\nSecond abort, and my mistake: I read _x0037__3 out of the export XML and took\nit for the JCR name. It is not. The exporter escapes any node name that is not\na legal XML element name, and an element name cannot start with a digit -- the\nrepository stores 7_3, with siblings 8_1 and 8_2. The home 404 page exporting\nas <_x0034_04> is the same escaping and confirms it.\n\nRoot is now documentation/jahia/7_3.\n\nSame correction in the guard, which matters more: the pattern added last commit\n(/_x003[89]__\\d) could never match a JCR path, so it protected nothing. Current\ndocs are documentation/jahia/8_1 and 8_2, now matched by /[89]_\\d. The dotted\njahia-8.x patterns are kept for titles and vanity URLs, where the dot is real.\n\nThe guard test now also asserts that the configured roots do not trip the guard\nthemselves, which is the check that would have caught this class of error\nwithout a round trip through the instance.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 3.0.8; guard passes 6 legacy paths, aborts on 9\ncurrent ones including bare 8_2, and both roots are clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAFgMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3k2hAf9GhPEslpQX9T8PBmGL84CD1qvxG8rwWTrTR2L87d2FnTBCXrnO+fSER/F\njgPJcRWzBQjicDFfeNFmi0Qd5veX8bLNNtUX7zosLl8o5ibArDkOlhVVnFBkKsaq\n8uR3VTAGs65fqQRO/ShY59b1zxjNOADDk0Dvjgzf1s77kKKOP43lZAzee21qBFjD\nlLyKIWlugxbEQrxplhQQW2tmSHpZBsxwZsqkA+4ymxhnECkuR25O06psCg3PPPtQ\nFlm2093xwmc7ymHquXt9MAr1HtkVBQMULzpUp85YFu3N5p+tDu0FzLIwcaDDfnFb\nVTFsFqpqAd0UaB5VhKNezseUj3skng==\n=IU1x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDcxZWZiMjBiNTc3OTFlZTM4MTE5ZmRiOTU2MTQ4M2RmZjI5NGJlZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277","sha":"2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277"}],"sha":"71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/71efb20b57791ee38119fdb9561483dff294beeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:32:48Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:37:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(scripts): use the real legacy roots, and make the guard see encoded names\n\nThe dry run aborted: none of the three assumed roots existed. Resolved them\nagainst the 2026-09-11 site export instead of guessing again.\n\nNone of the URL segments the prune recorded is a JCR path segment:\n\n  /archives/...                 -> a jnt:vanityUrl on the legacy-1 page, so the\n                                   127 /archives/ pages and the 537 legacy-1/\n                                   ones are one tree under two URL forms\n  /documentation/jahia-cms/...  -> jahia-cms exists nowhere in the repository;\n                                   it appears only inside vanity URLs\n\nRoots are now documentation/legacy-1 (781 jnt:page, titled \"Archives\", with\ndigital-experience-manager, marketing-factory, form-factory and the rest of the\nprune''s list as children) and documentation/jahia/_x0037__3 (217 jnt:page,\nagainst the prune''s 207 jahia-cms/jahia-7.x).\n\nThe guard needed the same correction, and this one mattered: JCR names are\nISO9075-encoded, so current docs sit at documentation/jahia/_x0038__1 and\n_x0038__2. The readable /jahia-8\\.\\d pattern could never match them -- the\nprotection for current content was not weak, it was absent. Added /_x003[89]__\\d\nand kept the readable patterns for titles and URLs.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 2.5.14 and 3.0.8; the guard, rebuilt from the\nscript''s own pattern list, passes 5 real legacy paths from the export and\naborts on 8 current ones including both encoded 8.x forms.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"af107b8f2f8789a7a62a325f80ac42d7ebf73625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/af107b8f2f8789a7a62a325f80ac42d7ebf73625"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277","verification":{"payload":"tree af107b8f2f8789a7a62a325f80ac42d7ebf73625\nparent c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790969568 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790973443 +0200\n\nfix(scripts): use the real legacy roots, and make the guard see encoded names\n\nThe dry run aborted: none of the three assumed roots existed. Resolved them\nagainst the 2026-09-11 site export instead of guessing again.\n\nNone of the URL segments the prune recorded is a JCR path segment:\n\n  /archives/...                 -> a jnt:vanityUrl on the legacy-1 page, so the\n                                   127 /archives/ pages and the 537 legacy-1/\n                                   ones are one tree under two URL forms\n  /documentation/jahia-cms/...  -> jahia-cms exists nowhere in the repository;\n                                   it appears only inside vanity URLs\n\nRoots are now documentation/legacy-1 (781 jnt:page, titled \"Archives\", with\ndigital-experience-manager, marketing-factory, form-factory and the rest of the\nprune''s list as children) and documentation/jahia/_x0037__3 (217 jnt:page,\nagainst the prune''s 207 jahia-cms/jahia-7.x).\n\nThe guard needed the same correction, and this one mattered: JCR names are\nISO9075-encoded, so current docs sit at documentation/jahia/_x0038__1 and\n_x0038__2. The readable /jahia-8\\.\\d pattern could never match them -- the\nprotection for current content was not weak, it was absent. Added /_x003[89]__\\d\nand kept the readable patterns for titles and URLs.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 2.5.14 and 3.0.8; the guard, rebuilt from the\nscript''s own pattern list, passes 5 real legacy paths from the export and\naborts on 8 current ones including both encoded 8.x forms.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAFgMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mzEgf/Q+s5MCGlJ75Jf0kOXXoJkSjZKCB9dRUtF5BPCq4FluRBpUoVgx4qjgRY\nYE7eyBwxTLeuCqlf2KfM5XB+bHo0TRgB6AURwyNb6GUnZ+JkRSA069CpYBIa8G45\neu73eL7W2HHs1mdq0rHbIbtaMoKRlQNpWTzSOcUo3TJgxk043MX7CqjIHgylysT8\npdr516qWmpmWFNMo6m+2ad923X9snJDUF2ZEYUOfcCBCC9BNSceewf1I30QvZjtf\nUCc8WYyTzaUMJyjhQF9d6Qg4DkloWs/EBjhhU84vVFwquV/AIrHDHWksnOTnFIE2\nSvnsl5Ui4N65WgG/1Z+KbXHJghfaQA==\n=XSev\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDI5MzM3OTVlNWEzOGQ1ZDhmYWE5OWZmM2M5MzlkYmE4YmEwOTAyNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c","sha":"c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c"}],"sha":"2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2933795e5a38d5d8faa99ff3c939dba8ba090277"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:00:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:37:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor(scripts): convert the skip-indexation script to Groovy\n\nReplaces the Node/GraphQL version with a Groovy script in the same shape as\ncleanup-legacy-customgpt-mixins.groovy: a system session per workspace, SQL2\ndiscovery, batched saves, run from the Groovy console or provisioning.\n\nRunning inside Jahia drops the whole remote surface -- no endpoint, no basic\nauth, no credential in the environment, no HTTP error handling -- and the two\nscripts that touch these mixins now work the same way.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: dry run by default, hard failure on a root that does\nnot resolve rather than a silent zero, the run aborts entirely if any selected\npath matches current content, already-marked nodes are skipped so re-runs are\nidempotent, and EDIT plus LIVE are both written because the listener binds to\nLIVE while EDIT keeps a later publish from undoing it.\n\nDiscovery now runs per workspace instead of once: a node can exist in one and\nnot the other, and each session should report what it can actually see.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 2.5.14 and 3.0.8, and the protected-path guard was\nexercised against 4 legacy paths that must be marked and 9 current paths that\nmust abort.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d8378630938cd515460344d36ac972b8ef09a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/9d8378630938cd515460344d36ac972b8ef09a82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d8378630938cd515460344d36ac972b8ef09a82\nparent 9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790967612 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790973443 +0200\n\nrefactor(scripts): convert the skip-indexation script to Groovy\n\nReplaces the Node/GraphQL version with a Groovy script in the same shape as\ncleanup-legacy-customgpt-mixins.groovy: a system session per workspace, SQL2\ndiscovery, batched saves, run from the Groovy console or provisioning.\n\nRunning inside Jahia drops the whole remote surface -- no endpoint, no basic\nauth, no credential in the environment, no HTTP error handling -- and the two\nscripts that touch these mixins now work the same way.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: dry run by default, hard failure on a root that does\nnot resolve rather than a silent zero, the run aborts entirely if any selected\npath matches current content, already-marked nodes are skipped so re-runs are\nidempotent, and EDIT plus LIVE are both written because the listener binds to\nLIVE while EDIT keeps a later publish from undoing it.\n\nDiscovery now runs per workspace instead of once: a node can exist in one and\nnot the other, and each session should report what it can actually see.\n\nVerified: parses on Groovy 2.5.14 and 3.0.8, and the protected-path guard was\nexercised against 4 legacy paths that must be marked and 9 current paths that\nmust abort.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAFgMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3njIQf/d3x0NgPSySjBQhe4SniiUa8o5qA8k6tSsw2ML4OvlmVPxgkss37UQXNh\njGrPYtS6gLU1Z0fNVt2whZGjtjhJSOPD0l0zwep9mpg18ITUJAJtaEjQoYMKnYTU\nALEISeUYHmRrv0/kJRGoj84Oe/k6erHmClOwxGP8MngbBwp2Hk8KF7t5Nh9kUVag\nYqpLN0ySCwJfnhd5FiUBuzaRg5Y8GaHduuK0XO2M5Z8RG/hg2Iagzrc7DmoluQ3Y\npHXs4qa9BlGNpPbSy6olaK5SS2DrVw/v0eG9QI4aVvkR2dpCdt0E0LjfotbEy1tx\nlRrC2fe+cbPGRjuiaOo/S1/3Jz9tjw==\n=OcU/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGM0OWQ2MzJjZmIzOWUzZjU3NjBiZDIwMzU5ODgxMWJlY2M3NDMwOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487","sha":"9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487"}],"sha":"c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/c49d632cfb39e3f5760bd203598811becc74309c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:56:41Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:37:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore(scripts): mark legacy content with the skip-indexation mixin\n\nThe 2026-09-30 prune deleted 912 obsolete pages from CustomGPT but changed\nnothing in Jahia, so every one of them still carries a customGptIndexable\nsidecar pointing at a now-deleted page id. One republish restores the\nlegacy content: the DELETE on the stale id returns 403, removeExistingPage()\ndiscards the boolean, and the POST proceeds.\n\nAdds jmix:skipCustomGptIndexation -- the module''s real opt-out, tested by\nService.skipIndexationForNode() -- through the standard JCR GraphQL\nmutation, in EDIT and in LIVE.\n\nLIVE as well as EDIT because IndexerJCRListener binds to LIVE and the index\nbuilder reads LIVE, so a mixin only in EDIT does nothing until the page is\npublished -- and publishing 912 archived pages would push whatever drafts\nsit beside them. Writing LIVE directly keeps the blast radius to this mixin.\n\nDry run by default, writes a durable manifest (the prune''s manifest lived in\na scratchpad and is gone, which is why the roots now have to be rediscovered),\nhard-fails on a root that does not resolve rather than marking nothing, and\naborts the whole run if any selected path matches current content.\n\nNote it does NOT strip jmix:customGptIndexable: the indexer adds that itself\nto host the sidecar, so removing it would drop the page id and make the next\nrepublish POST a duplicate with nothing left to clean it up by.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d19f652fe8a85af9ee835de64088df4038b4341e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/d19f652fe8a85af9ee835de64088df4038b4341e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487","verification":{"payload":"tree d19f652fe8a85af9ee835de64088df4038b4341e\nparent 82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790967401 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790973443 +0200\n\nchore(scripts): mark legacy content with the skip-indexation mixin\n\nThe 2026-09-30 prune deleted 912 obsolete pages from CustomGPT but changed\nnothing in Jahia, so every one of them still carries a customGptIndexable\nsidecar pointing at a now-deleted page id. One republish restores the\nlegacy content: the DELETE on the stale id returns 403, removeExistingPage()\ndiscards the boolean, and the POST proceeds.\n\nAdds jmix:skipCustomGptIndexation -- the module''s real opt-out, tested by\nService.skipIndexationForNode() -- through the standard JCR GraphQL\nmutation, in EDIT and in LIVE.\n\nLIVE as well as EDIT because IndexerJCRListener binds to LIVE and the index\nbuilder reads LIVE, so a mixin only in EDIT does nothing until the page is\npublished -- and publishing 912 archived pages would push whatever drafts\nsit beside them. Writing LIVE directly keeps the blast radius to this mixin.\n\nDry run by default, writes a durable manifest (the prune''s manifest lived in\na scratchpad and is gone, which is why the roots now have to be rediscovered),\nhard-fails on a root that does not resolve rather than marking nothing, and\naborts the whole run if any selected path matches current content.\n\nNote it does NOT strip jmix:customGptIndexable: the indexer adds that itself\nto host the sidecar, so removing it would drop the page id and make the next\nrepublish POST a duplicate with nothing left to clean it up by.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmrAFgMACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kBOAgAiaeKOFP5czJENrwtBC2yxKSWWYLXY0irNqRaOE5sNr4j0VNI2eMBi0/T\nvIPcvPIO7lwRMjSubb3x2MPzF3Rf4AqD1ql4RId4vIQ07uckSu1LxhZCM3HBJ3GY\nITvg6PZXx8lyX1Pibvb57infNL+fGE8FcowAf2d7pwcZW74k1sxAB+M6G6EBMqtN\nynW1/VAfRPnDpgnvD2iIM5EQK16p6PqLImWEYdSCETbLHyapzFaPG6Lbd+h7tJKa\ndREyxlOx1gAjizHmCK0fMqXsB7e/SBRImUi+C7dLZmFEUlyKRiiVedUMjW+Z2KFK\nCEEU7pt3/rE9p0VpyfVk+6anvtP4yg==\n=tXNr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T20:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDlkZjYwOTdiODUyMWZiZDAxYjQxMTBhM2Y1NDgzMDNkYTUwNTA0ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f","sha":"82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/82b50ec41a3343bbea24102070534b51958aed9f"}],"sha":"9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9df6097b8521fbd01b4110a3f548303da5050487"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https