N PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmq+GagACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kM9gf8ChTJK5NkY4yo/jq/9Hm0z8lmhAM55cdEp+eTwpEVJB4DUX7q8/BSGKTU\nUGqG13X6nNI8d1lGKHNnhAafhw9eGqc0DK/79ixis+KZ6VIraCQpDr4CaZLrUOlK\n1SWDeIN94KwNbSCy5kI27uH9CMtgrIl3a1Uy++yQyUr0Cz7wFHkNMJOzd7SjW5Fe\ndBNxf2VB46VTNYzJs8BpVkrQGC2LFeuUjYkFd5Lv14l5WXhZINBCytKrpNnVKXuf\ngFhP46MJ3EBgVzrhpOc9oaGF3gUg8gexsQWfm6m5j9HZJluIY10Vmr3KjALI/5cV\nNrAif8Hsr55eRtvwbrFrJ/U7IA9zYA==\n=zFMA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T08:29:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/3b0da4b81a03f43e7e80f495439bdbdec75ff651","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDNiMGRhNGI4MWEwM2Y0M2U3ZTgwZjQ5NTQzOWJkYmRlYzc1ZmY2NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d","sha":"9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d"}],"sha":"3b0da4b81a03f43e7e80f495439bdbdec75ff651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/3b0da4b81a03f43e7e80f495439bdbdec75ff651"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:48:36Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:48:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: give the orphan report the context a human needs to judge it (#33)\n\nDeliberately no redundancy predicate. The evidence that separated residue from\nunique content on this corpus was a CONSTANT byte delta repeating down a\ncluster - 19617 across five ''Spring Bean modifications'' pages, ~9235 across\nthree ''Upgrade ... on Jahia Cloud'' ones - and that pattern is legible only when\nthe rows are read side by side. A boolean would have thrown it away.\n\nAn exact-URL predicate could only ever have answered ''not redundant'': 47 of the\n65 orphans carry no URL at all. Measured by content instead, ~49 of 65 are older\nrenders of pages that are still claimed, and 16 are genuinely unique.\n\nEach orphan now reports its size, its single claimed title-twin with that page''s\nsize, and a probable node path. Specifically:\n\n- filesize comes from the listing, which carries it as an integer on all 1920\n  records of the corpus this was written against. Every one of those is\n  is_file: true, so a crawled page has never been observed; a missing value is\n  reported as ''unknown'' rather than assumed to be anything.\n- A title twin is reported only when exactly ONE claimed page shares the title.\n  This corpus has ''Overview'' x13 and ''Introduction'' x10; one of thirteen is not\n  evidence, and showing it as a twin would invite exactly the wrong deletion.\n- The node path is labelled a guess. A URL path beginning /home/, /contents/ or\n  /files/ is a raw JCR path; anything else is a vanity URL, which has no\n  reliable inverse, so no hint is printed for it. That covers 8 of the 18\n  URL-bearing orphans and stays silent on the other 10.\n\nsiteKey is accepted only to render that hint. The sweep itself stays\nproject-wide, because scoping it to one site would classify every other site''s\npages as orphaned.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"70d4bed258a4901ab24eda9672bd553ca40fb929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/70d4bed258a4901ab24eda9672bd553ca40fb929"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d","verification":{"payload":"tree 70d4bed258a4901ab24eda9672bd553ca40fb929\nparent 664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790801316 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790801316 +0200\n\nfeat: give the orphan report the context a human needs to judge it (#33)\n\nDeliberately no redundancy predicate. The evidence that separated residue from\nunique content on this corpus was a CONSTANT byte delta repeating down a\ncluster - 19617 across five ''Spring Bean modifications'' pages, ~9235 across\nthree ''Upgrade ... on Jahia Cloud'' ones - and that pattern is legible only when\nthe rows are read side by side. A boolean would have thrown it away.\n\nAn exact-URL predicate could only ever have answered ''not redundant'': 47 of the\n65 orphans carry no URL at all. Measured by content instead, ~49 of 65 are older\nrenders of pages that are still claimed, and 16 are genuinely unique.\n\nEach orphan now reports its size, its single claimed title-twin with that page''s\nsize, and a probable node path. Specifically:\n\n- filesize comes from the listing, which carries it as an integer on all 1920\n  records of the corpus this was written against. Every one of those is\n  is_file: true, so a crawled page has never been observed; a missing value is\n  reported as ''unknown'' rather than assumed to be anything.\n- A title twin is reported only when exactly ONE claimed page shares the title.\n  This corpus has ''Overview'' x13 and ''Introduction'' x10; one of thirteen is not\n  evidence, and showing it as a twin would invite exactly the wrong deletion.\n- The node path is labelled a guess. A URL path beginning /home/, /contents/ or\n  /files/ is a raw JCR path; anything else is a vanity URL, which has no\n  reliable inverse, so no hint is printed for it. That covers 8 of the 18\n  URL-bearing orphans and stays silent on the other 10.\n\nsiteKey is accepted only to render that hint. The sweep itself stays\nproject-wide, because scoping it to one site would classify every other site''s\npages as orphaned.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXWkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFywQABQQG0gnfXjgO+4RtXZeYr1e\nG7zPyIzUtpYyMBSWpmfaeT8BcIylFq58jbucwskQegjow2uBfzaEJNRTRkkE6PzM\nqLTR7+/35CJqYfubmIANszI9JG9JTaIieW+d1AQ1pDvZJSQNP/vqY317keff4fzx\nG4hTebF+Z88C5ajzAn7vqKb2yiOU8OaXCoUubAZe9Pq8cqHp/EQha+ar9jigLNQy\nDcNTC2/LWxtWXOGVuibOWvaTcSm9jIhXutHhky3BW3caCbE84+mtSMC84Iq+Oqab\n+8jPm19nn57f9y2BPBW98qIfj7s7XS18DiipNkg3NLsWE9zXEKrYKX4GT8E549A7\nBmGVMNE1jezIeWdCRAYRZ4RsEPqtyo9w2/skqzfUzj1YzK2kimKMKLLHQ9Ykt8wP\ndiSarlxgCuhcf8SPpqfRh5INz3atnVA5zjf3SvwU+rjdVYIicUiZ24L2g8vCUojI\nty2jDVVwZsFLMjCLF2R0R5qIAgNRECDWKo92Z9IDASqApLwfbhflodle4xJ2BOa0\niU3cU1ptHrQ47xY2Xoh1hummcOd4MQqP2jfbJkthohsGdc4ybryKJDpIrszsxYX3\nKM4LJ+xv9pxMzi/4AD/9FbOqq4zkQDAgqxJ2LBEQo6wZRLIfoXiQlxD7G/rklCkL\nQbDrZ9nHyooI5QwTFiim\n=I0vp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:48:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDk4ODdlYmZjNGI4NzM0OWE4YzdhODZhYWY5M2ZjNDUyOTY0YTRiMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b","sha":"664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b"}],"sha":"9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9887ebfc4b87349a8c7a86aaf93fc452964a4b1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:41:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:41:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: never delete orphaned pages wholesale, and report their real URLs (#32)\n\nMeasured on production: of 65 orphans, ZERO were redundant. 18 held substantive\nunique content - CVE analyses, SBOMs, VEX documents, security advisories,\ncompatibility matrices, documentation landing pages - with working citation\nlinks. A wholesale sweep would have removed all of it from the corpus.\n\nThe detection is sound. The remedy was not. A page no mapping node claims has\ntwo causes with opposite remedies:\n\n  - content deleted in Jahia, and the page is residue to remove;\n  - the mapping node lost while the content survives, and the page is the ONLY\n    copy of that content. Deleting it destroys it; the remedy is to re-index the\n    node so it regains a mapping.\n\nTelling them apart needs the stored URL of every claimed page, which is\nthousands of metadata reads and cannot be done inside one request. So the tool\nno longer guesses: deletion requires an explicit pageIds list that a human has\nread and passed back, and naming an id that is not an orphan does not make it\ndeletable.\n\nThe log was actively arguing for the wrong decision. Every orphan printed\nurl=null, because the URL was read from the pages LISTING, which reports null\nfor every uploaded page in this corpus - all is_file: true with an empty\npage_url. That made each orphan look like an empty husk when 18 of 20 sampled\nhad real URLs. Orphans are now enriched from the per-page metadata endpoint,\nthrough the corroborating read, and the report states plainly that an orphan is\nnot necessarily redundant and how to tell.\n\nA tool whose output misleads a careful operator into destroying content is worse\nthan no tool. This one did.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b288b7d7545f4782ae6640c24f9accf24d2022e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/9b288b7d7545f4782ae6640c24f9accf24d2022e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b288b7d7545f4782ae6640c24f9accf24d2022e\nparent ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790800872 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790800872 +0200\n\nfix: never delete orphaned pages wholesale, and report their real URLs (#32)\n\nMeasured on production: of 65 orphans, ZERO were redundant. 18 held substantive\nunique content - CVE analyses, SBOMs, VEX documents, security advisories,\ncompatibility matrices, documentation landing pages - with working citation\nlinks. A wholesale sweep would have removed all of it from the corpus.\n\nThe detection is sound. The remedy was not. A page no mapping node claims has\ntwo causes with opposite remedies:\n\n  - content deleted in Jahia, and the page is residue to remove;\n  - the mapping node lost while the content survives, and the page is the ONLY\n    copy of that content. Deleting it destroys it; the remedy is to re-index the\n    node so it regains a mapping.\n\nTelling them apart needs the stored URL of every claimed page, which is\nthousands of metadata reads and cannot be done inside one request. So the tool\nno longer guesses: deletion requires an explicit pageIds list that a human has\nread and passed back, and naming an id that is not an orphan does not make it\ndeletable.\n\nThe log was actively arguing for the wrong decision. Every orphan printed\nurl=null, because the URL was read from the pages LISTING, which reports null\nfor every uploaded page in this corpus - all is_file: true with an empty\npage_url. That made each orphan look like an empty husk when 18 of 20 sampled\nhad real URLs. Orphans are now enriched from the per-page metadata endpoint,\nthrough the corroborating read, and the report states plainly that an orphan is\nnot necessarily redundant and how to tell.\n\nA tool whose output misleads a careful operator into destroying content is worse\nthan no tool. This one did.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXPoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvEsQAKTuUOH98jKZ3surO/h6H1uc\nMCM3rNqyZ8kcRD+m7JsIyeeczrR5yANIamGck2OZPkWwHUjClEc4h+1zdHgydx9J\nkxsMI9bkwawM5HJV1W2v9Qy0xY7HhTVYh9l+FFVreefspDBsUFTxCqvZm8Sj6GjM\ny3LYLC6YH5X2sq1iEv7yucFgjTlwKTR21BJ6vjeAiUFHuCHNYvrjyTE/X1NMV4XZ\nnoBPBBaZ+5tgLdbelNAVoj5VMBnl4E411MtgQmoPy7pxnpqokAAtJCPhOhuPrcbH\nk6uIlvFWMagEheADW3AKIer8WnpOrWA1bQph7cZM9CsYBfASXB+mpsx62lWW1hO9\ndAW8kl3Vz7RIJARUJIsQbfp57J7gy4/OGwERJRtxIylhoIvQ0mwU76hb4ep/6eNf\n7CK5h96wqv94VGoBAVDjsjpVTUPZhOnkeEhQNFr6Tnu/Qpo0draXuNUOTedoRgx2\nLxkoMkldxyADq3n+Y1TvMS+34jMKbYgfxtPGkgyr7CCqKOknEfUju6jYx4MVfuLu\nmGZwzR4OsWLiSDdDSQ2QJ+lVPmJR91gzb9BAkgWAdkUoahc57YE0VZrzJhYLCo/G\n7O/NbAxbXYrFj/XcqfEu8tapDi2lNZOAAZwBCozYUu/6afnfORPflX+fTm/u08y3\nClNWigCGsn7QanjUEocY\n=4wN0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:41:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDY2NGM4YTE1MTE3MTFiNTE5Y2Y0MmNjZTQzMDFjNjVhZjNiZDJkMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5","sha":"ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5"}],"sha":"664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/664c8a1511711b519cf42cce4301c65af3bd2d1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:20:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:20:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: skip the plan-size guard when the caller named the page ids (#31)\n\nThe plan-size guard asks what share of a population looks wrong, which is the\nsignal that catches a systematically wrong computation across a whole site.\nAgainst an explicit pageIds list there is no population: the caller has already\nmade the selection the guard exists to sanity-check.\n\nSo for any batch consisting purely of repair targets,\n\n    plan / examined = N / N = 100%\n\nregardless of batch size. Batching changes N, never the ratio. The only way to\nsatisfy a 25% threshold would be padding every call with healthy pages - 25\ntargets plus 75 that need nothing - which is an operator deliberately feeding a\nguard false negatives to get past it. That is worse than not having the guard,\nbecause it trains working around a refusal rather than reading it.\n\nThe guard still applies to an unscoped whole-site run, where the question it\nasks is meaningful.\n\nThe per-page checks are untouched and fire in both modes: assertUrlUsable, the\nnull-segment refusal and the host comparison judge each value on its own merits,\nindependently of how the target set was chosen. Those are what stopped the\nlocale defect, not the plan-size check.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d800318fc41ed4e209299c7229a8034e3bcd63a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/d800318fc41ed4e209299c7229a8034e3bcd63a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5","verification":{"payload":"tree d800318fc41ed4e209299c7229a8034e3bcd63a7\nparent 9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790799635 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790799635 +0200\n\nfix: skip the plan-size guard when the caller named the page ids (#31)\n\nThe plan-size guard asks what share of a population looks wrong, which is the\nsignal that catches a systematically wrong computation across a whole site.\nAgainst an explicit pageIds list there is no population: the caller has already\nmade the selection the guard exists to sanity-check.\n\nSo for any batch consisting purely of repair targets,\n\n    plan / examined = N / N = 100%\n\nregardless of batch size. Batching changes N, never the ratio. The only way to\nsatisfy a 25% threshold would be padding every call with healthy pages - 25\ntargets plus 75 that need nothing - which is an operator deliberately feeding a\nguard false negatives to get past it. That is worse than not having the guard,\nbecause it trains working around a refusal rather than reading it.\n\nThe guard still applies to an unscoped whole-site run, where the question it\nasks is meaningful.\n\nThe per-page checks are untouched and fire in both modes: assertUrlUsable, the\nnull-segment refusal and the host comparison judge each value on its own merits,\nindependently of how the target set was chosen. Those are what stopped the\nlocale defect, not the plan-size check.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvW8TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAENgQACAsQnenoMqiORKFlqXR5ai+\nBzS/id8OGoV8OYQmJz0rBPKLW/dGTfYx29Ab55rD8d2WlNgNVljfrHE/aw33s9IB\nlZq4TAGTSWabgu8aZDUo6C1uOfw8hJ5TmGbRBW0HZJ7ZA13TN5ZHDQ0aBBw2oBVN\nCMPXZAVIKjeNKjl056ccmN3iUMbm7M/jkwTD7hZwiK+egz640UKYlA0dA2mHsg+H\nZ5CSIm07QTXFXvfwCG6afiZ3ZBLp69yBBhSSDhZfEfVr3uiRwG0+e2TZRUaXNUR+\nKBKsVyhP8VLEJ/FUkrkBtytKLcYpIIq6LJh+vc/TEFKYsTWnm5AlDm/0kMVB/K1d\ne48ZEooP2pPPJjMPy7pAbynOfggqasjvVKOs1a4Ynzd1b6vuKiizTlsmOu5wAAQv\n+DNHj3E4Eo5f3B/uKF/5Huot9d3X7MFw2NODP6pV7YV7GUM17ATvTk+fpEqjzmkr\no339KtM7F4OWSk26/gK+kSw8MgebgXzJz+5NOwa51Gz5/L38+tn9pvSGCfTdrvZW\nNcAh5TLIvaDsH0khMT9Hhcf0BhBBba5kzxHVZhtKAVB9mludMYEqB1jQfYHaOIk9\n4TTdvzRqP8RZUd/o+7o+AA9yRtv4GhtfP/3ELGFucxDvX/jXlMT7To9drwb7hHYe\ncRQI1pd1ATlUnBllZkK2\n=3zzL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:20:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGNhODlmMmVlY2ExMDYwNzM3N2I0NzNkNTYxMjM1OWMyMjMzMmE3YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a","sha":"9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a"}],"sha":"ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/ca89f2eeca10607377b473d5612359c22332a7a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:14:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:14:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: bound the URL repair to one request, scope it by page id, and corroborate reads (#30)\n\nThree defects, all found by running the dry run against the rebuilt snapshot.\n\n1. The repair could not complete. repairSite runs synchronously on the caller''s\n   HTTP request thread and walks ~2784 mapping nodes at roughly 0.6s each - 25 to\n   30 minutes. The request died at ~91s and the client received an HTML error\n   page instead of JSON.\n\n   This is worse than a timeout. The client giving up does not stop the server,\n   so with dryRun:false the run would keep rewriting an unknown subset, silently,\n   with no summary and no returned count. assertRunIsBounded now refuses a run\n   above 100 pages rather than starting one that cannot finish.\n\n2. Nothing could scope the run. repairPageUrls takes an optional pageIds list,\n   which turns 2784 examinations into the 58 confirmed targets and finishes\n   inside a request comfortably.\n\n3. The data.id echo check is necessary but not sufficient. The API was observed\n   returning {status:success,data:{id:<the right id>,...,url:null}} for\n   a page confirmed by direct call to have a URL: correct envelope, dropped\n   payload. A single read therefore manufactures a rewrite target for a page that\n   was already correct - which is how a 6-worker pass produced 2558 false nulls -\n   and makes a successful write look like a failure during verification.\n\n   readStoredUrl reads twice before believing a missing value. The degradation\n   drops values rather than inventing them, so corroboration is asymmetric: a\n   value seen in ANY read is real, only a value absent from every read is\n   believed absent. A response naming a different page is still rejected\n   outright, since that is not a dropped value.\n\n   One consequence is visible in the tests: a dropped read no longer answers with\n   a second write against an API that drops writes under load.\n\nWhole-site runs need this to become a background job, which is not in this\nchange; until then, scope with pageIds in batches.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d561c31c5afe7a552ec02aff5ed912a172379385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/d561c31c5afe7a552ec02aff5ed912a172379385"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a","verification":{"payload":"tree d561c31c5afe7a552ec02aff5ed912a172379385\nparent fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790799278 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790799278 +0200\n\nfix: bound the URL repair to one request, scope it by page id, and corroborate reads (#30)\n\nThree defects, all found by running the dry run against the rebuilt snapshot.\n\n1. The repair could not complete. repairSite runs synchronously on the caller''s\n   HTTP request thread and walks ~2784 mapping nodes at roughly 0.6s each - 25 to\n   30 minutes. The request died at ~91s and the client received an HTML error\n   page instead of JSON.\n\n   This is worse than a timeout. The client giving up does not stop the server,\n   so with dryRun:false the run would keep rewriting an unknown subset, silently,\n   with no summary and no returned count. assertRunIsBounded now refuses a run\n   above 100 pages rather than starting one that cannot finish.\n\n2. Nothing could scope the run. repairPageUrls takes an optional pageIds list,\n   which turns 2784 examinations into the 58 confirmed targets and finishes\n   inside a request comfortably.\n\n3. The data.id echo check is necessary but not sufficient. The API was observed\n   returning {status:success,data:{id:<the right id>,...,url:null}} for\n   a page confirmed by direct call to have a URL: correct envelope, dropped\n   payload. A single read therefore manufactures a rewrite target for a page that\n   was already correct - which is how a 6-worker pass produced 2558 false nulls -\n   and makes a successful write look like a failure during verification.\n\n   readStoredUrl reads twice before believing a missing value. The degradation\n   drops values rather than inventing them, so corroboration is asymmetric: a\n   value seen in ANY read is real, only a value absent from every read is\n   believed absent. A response naming a different page is still rejected\n   outright, since that is not a dropped value.\n\n   One consequence is visible in the tests: a dropped read no longer answers with\n   a second write against an API that drops writes under load.\n\nWhole-site runs need this to become a background job, which is not in this\nchange; until then, scope with pageIds in batches.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvW2vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVwUQADdos8N+gYAtPOGA5Vb2yP6g\nnb55qXqbenXdvvJswyh5ktViYBPdYKEnOA9D74WYVcxqL3Hm5HfrAfpvV07MsY05\nyJR+NBQc49fA8bCSmh1pjcUTlJEPjk80M5WayQnpU3MTKwAg7D+r3mGvwGhjq/R1\n+WWJZz0aHfhtEdCUf5b/KX40g7i/jVLyks5NP+LQ/3TBCSqy4qyFnytfoirl/SwL\nnuXsxUju9rJtt0a8rsBg5KsVPzFP0Ev5Fgw4QqmU8TIJn9+2AXODpV9x/bxJZvlm\n7uok8kbVS3qdZt7A3kfwjm7/4j/EgnN3KfRgSdQZPZPb/CGeefjTA9xjotpXH8sU\nhw4hX3Q2xjbafUJc9tOhIvuVO2urMlILWwZX4voF64Vr2YxLvuTaPs4uxw6/3fkm\n0stlmA/0Er2kJ+QUWIEjaEMt7jJbvfN8rBo0Lv/cRKcFpXpZqvR4z9sgMp4DoeXh\nXlWoYxP7DD1wlKTOFVZGkHMfXO+0Bj1NRyfp1NnLxHPw1dmvNLa20TScY+v8I3jz\nlw6Z3Q4J53SbHWddZHP+wVy/kPYUtePZRaLgs5FQ7c6lEmLld8aq2kxg/iQpwQ07\nIwcJ8KEQbpfgi7khV/4VhW3pqRSqZXwuZij79U9o73V5aVWkyYxXfVDbH3+NvbKN\nHNNd4Uk/UDBLN9XsuME1\n=v3tk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:14:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDkyODNjZGNhYTcyODJmM2YyOWJkYWMxMTBjOGViNjdjOWNhZDA5MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c","sha":"fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c"}],"sha":"9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/9283cdcaa7282f3f29bdac110c8eb67c9cad091a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:15:06Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:15:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: find and remove CustomGPT pages that no Jahia content claims (#29)\n\n* feat: find and remove CustomGPT pages that no Jahia content claims\n\nRoughly 60 pages in the production corpus answer 404 on their stored URL -\ncontent indexed and then removed or moved without the corpus being updated,\nincluding a security advisory. Their URL is present, just dead, so PageUrlRepair\nleaves them alone: the remedy is deleting the page, not rewriting its URL.\n\nDetection is a repository fact rather than a network observation. Mapping nodes\nare children of the content node, so deleting content deletes its mapping; a\nproject page whose id no mapping node holds is a page nothing in Jahia accounts\nfor. Probing URLs for a 404 would instead flag the ~27% of the corpus behind\nauth, whose status cannot be observed anonymously, and would depend on the\nacademy being reachable at the moment of the sweep.\n\nThis is also how a page gets orphaned in the first place: the delete never\npropagated. The stale-listener defect in JAHIACOM-1675 is exactly that failure\nmode, and a failed delete used to be discarded silently.\n\nTwo safety properties, because the blast radius is the whole corpus:\n\n- The mapping-node query is repository-wide, NOT scoped to a site. A project may\n  hold pages from more than one site - a store.jahia.com page reached the academy\n  corpus before the registration gate existed - and scoping to one site would\n  classify every other site''s pages as orphaned.\n- The sweep refuses to run when Jahia holds no mapping nodes at all, since that\n  would classify every page as orphaned. An empty result is far more likely to be\n  a failed query or a partially restored repository than a genuinely empty index,\n  and the corpus cannot be recovered from it.\n\nExposed as sweepOrphanedPages(dryRun), gated on customgpt-admin and audit-logged.\ndryRun is a required argument rather than a defaulted one, so the destructive\nchoice is always explicit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: do not report a mapping node pointing at a deleted page as a repair failure\n\n~1138 pages were removed from the production project directly through the API -\n223 duplicates, 912 obsolete pages, the two failed documents and one foreign-site\npage - without Jahia being involved. That many mapping nodes now hold a\ncustomGptPageId pointing at a page that no longer exists.\n\nfetchPageMetadata threw a plain IOException for those, so a URL repair run would\nhave reported every one as a failure, burying the handful that are genuinely\nactionable under thousands that are not.\n\nfetchPageMetadata now raises PageGoneException for 403 and 404 - this API answers\n403 for an id it does not know, not 404 - and PageUrlRepair counts those apart\nand logs them at DEBUG. The run summary now reports them as their own category.\n\nA dangling mapping node is cosmetic and self-healing: the next publication\nre-indexes the node, and since the delete treats an absent page as gone, it no\nlonger orphans a replacement. Pre-#26 it would have silently added a duplicate\ninstead, which is a neat illustration of why that fix mattered.\n\nPageGoneException extends IOException so callers that do not distinguish keep\nworking - verifyStoredMetadata in particular treats a page vanishing mid-write\nas the genuine failure it is.\n\nThe orphan sweep is unaffected in either direction: it enumerates project pages,\nso a mapping node the project does not match simply never appears.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: stop the URL repair writing a null locale into page URLs, and guard the write\n\nPageUrlRepair opened its JCR session with a NULL locale. JCRNodeWrapper.getUrl()\nrenders the session locale into the path, so it produced the literal string\n''null'' as a path segment and the repair wrote\n\n  https://<host>/null/<jcr-path>.html\n\nover URLs that were correct. Every page it touched became a 404. This ran on\nproduction before being stopped mid-run.\n\nThe indexer path was never affected: it opens the session with\nLocale.forLanguageTag(language). The fault was introduced when resolvePublicUrl\nwas extracted to be shared by both paths without carrying over the argument that\nmade it correct. The repair now resolves the site''s default language once and\nopens every session with it, and refuses outright when a site has no default\nlanguage rather than writing an unresolved segment.\n\nThree guards, because the read-back cannot help here and never could: it proves\na value was STORED, not that it is RIGHT. Writing a corrupt URL and reading the\nsame corrupt URL back passes the data.id and data.url checks perfectly.\n\n1. assertUrlUsable rejects, before any write, a URL that does not parse, has no\n   host, contains a path segment equal to ''null'', or disagrees with the stored\n   URL on the host. A move changes the path, not the host.\n2. repairSite is now two-phase. The examine phase writes nothing, so a dry run\n   reports exactly what a real run would do, and the plan is sized before\n   anything is written.\n3. assertPlanIsPlausible refuses a plan covering more than 25% of examined pages.\n   That catches the shape no per-URL check can: a computation producing a\n   plausible but wrong URL for everything, indistinguishable from a mass move.\n\ndryRun is now a required argument on repairPageUrls rather than absent, so the\ndestructive choice is always explicit - matching sweepOrphanedPages. The exact\ncomparison that widened the blast radius from ~79 pages to the whole corpus is\nkept, because convergence is still right; it is the unguarded write that was\nwrong.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"06cbe2b7c7edba3cc4ff484ef9c01cdc7198c865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/06cbe2b7c7edba3cc4ff484ef9c01cdc7198c865"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 06cbe2b7c7edba3cc4ff484ef9c01cdc7198c865\nparent 13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790795706 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790795706 +0200\n\nfeat: find and remove CustomGPT pages that no Jahia content claims (#29)\n\n* feat: find and remove CustomGPT pages that no Jahia content claims\n\nRoughly 60 pages in the production corpus answer 404 on their stored URL -\ncontent indexed and then removed or moved without the corpus being updated,\nincluding a security advisory. Their URL is present, just dead, so PageUrlRepair\nleaves them alone: the remedy is deleting the page, not rewriting its URL.\n\nDetection is a repository fact rather than a network observation. Mapping nodes\nare children of the content node, so deleting content deletes its mapping; a\nproject page whose id no mapping node holds is a page nothing in Jahia accounts\nfor. Probing URLs for a 404 would instead flag the ~27% of the corpus behind\nauth, whose status cannot be observed anonymously, and would depend on the\nacademy being reachable at the moment of the sweep.\n\nThis is also how a page gets orphaned in the first place: the delete never\npropagated. The stale-listener defect in JAHIACOM-1675 is exactly that failure\nmode, and a failed delete used to be discarded silently.\n\nTwo safety properties, because the blast radius is the whole corpus:\n\n- The mapping-node query is repository-wide, NOT scoped to a site. A project may\n  hold pages from more than one site - a store.jahia.com page reached the academy\n  corpus before the registration gate existed - and scoping to one site would\n  classify every other site''s pages as orphaned.\n- The sweep refuses to run when Jahia holds no mapping nodes at all, since that\n  would classify every page as orphaned. An empty result is far more likely to be\n  a failed query or a partially restored repository than a genuinely empty index,\n  and the corpus cannot be recovered from it.\n\nExposed as sweepOrphanedPages(dryRun), gated on customgpt-admin and audit-logged.\ndryRun is a required argument rather than a defaulted one, so the destructive\nchoice is always explicit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: do not report a mapping node pointing at a deleted page as a repair failure\n\n~1138 pages were removed from the production project directly through the API -\n223 duplicates, 912 obsolete pages, the two failed documents and one foreign-site\npage - without Jahia being involved. That many mapping nodes now hold a\ncustomGptPageId pointing at a page that no longer exists.\n\nfetchPageMetadata threw a plain IOException for those, so a URL repair run would\nhave reported every one as a failure, burying the handful that are genuinely\nactionable under thousands that are not.\n\nfetchPageMetadata now raises PageGoneException for 403 and 404 - this API answers\n403 for an id it does not know, not 404 - and PageUrlRepair counts those apart\nand logs them at DEBUG. The run summary now reports them as their own category.\n\nA dangling mapping node is cosmetic and self-healing: the next publication\nre-indexes the node, and since the delete treats an absent page as gone, it no\nlonger orphans a replacement. Pre-#26 it would have silently added a duplicate\ninstead, which is a neat illustration of why that fix mattered.\n\nPageGoneException extends IOException so callers that do not distinguish keep\nworking - verifyStoredMetadata in particular treats a page vanishing mid-write\nas the genuine failure it is.\n\nThe orphan sweep is unaffected in either direction: it enumerates project pages,\nso a mapping node the project does not match simply never appears.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: stop the URL repair writing a null locale into page URLs, and guard the write\n\nPageUrlRepair opened its JCR session with a NULL locale. JCRNodeWrapper.getUrl()\nrenders the session locale into the path, so it produced the literal string\n''null'' as a path segment and the repair wrote\n\n  https://<host>/null/<jcr-path>.html\n\nover URLs that were correct. Every page it touched became a 404. This ran on\nproduction before being stopped mid-run.\n\nThe indexer path was never affected: it opens the session with\nLocale.forLanguageTag(language). The fault was introduced when resolvePublicUrl\nwas extracted to be shared by both paths without carrying over the argument that\nmade it correct. The repair now resolves the site''s default language once and\nopens every session with it, and refuses outright when a site has no default\nlanguage rather than writing an unresolved segment.\n\nThree guards, because the read-back cannot help here and never could: it proves\na value was STORED, not that it is RIGHT. Writing a corrupt URL and reading the\nsame corrupt URL back passes the data.id and data.url checks perfectly.\n\n1. assertUrlUsable rejects, before any write, a URL that does not parse, has no\n   host, contains a path segment equal to ''null'', or disagrees with the stored\n   URL on the host. A move changes the path, not the host.\n2. repairSite is now two-phase. The examine phase writes nothing, so a dry run\n   reports exactly what a real run would do, and the plan is sized before\n   anything is written.\n3. assertPlanIsPlausible refuses a plan covering more than 25% of examined pages.\n   That catches the shape no per-URL check can: a computation producing a\n   plausible but wrong URL for everything, indistinguishable from a mass move.\n\ndryRun is now a required argument on repairPageUrls rather than absent, so the\ndestructive choice is always explicit - matching sweepOrphanedPages. The exact\ncomparison that widened the blast radius from ~79 pages to the whole corpus is\nkept, because convergence is still right; it is the unguarded write that was\nwrong.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvV+6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtcEQAEd3mGKwjXDdljQwfciYl0Wl\nxeWUd+39W5J/OIOmQc1xxMV+rx4hoIRsbOaP0nvADNZkgU0I/llrBqxCAMYq1+9/\n7q+1r/6jun45EYDzv7KYrYeK10sgCjHGfr+QVZ4DwWzmLGgkc0jnrUCdXjkJ/DKx\nMvOzCrSiejE0n2otlXb0vcDugTGs3RF8CKOG6nr1/SFnwNSs0Quym9vg9CuDDdTd\nyvAnm2Jnc5I94IaN++rHXh0feTKqvCobme7RUdmPbSS5Ia7bgz4IdkYTSvuAohmY\nUU3yEzMtngHLCk42MvUZLnbPg4mkk/g8dHevQ/zKl7Kj/2W/ZRqtwTwwtGS9OklW\nZufo//ZIfwcag7/EZRx4qZHXTrD0VYBu2mY31DVVLJLrPVcYQhDkFAyk5r+NgKZc\nBYgWKnxVSAZI2jttxNLbpHZ9CWT+ELtaEAwGHcRjYKtmOFu5jjMHWYFU7Megat5y\nZxKJ0qcfeSSzuj5+epaAESaN2Y4YO2EF6QvPcgF5OHGzls4s08OHrs/BWBc/89Qw\n1BKzjinnMxOSJ9KeWi3KbKeUD46/IcDhqyX2sVVWj5bjXFZcPPvamjf3nayxPUEA\nGQlzZCGaco8pTwTdaPocKjKIymE84uugwXNd2+vyqovydgkTEYN9QagxMUuFewu1\nwTm6YKa88VxrwnAW0ZOK\n=Cdnv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T19:15:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKGZlNWZjZjA4MjgwMjhlZDhhMjg3MDg3Njk2NDI3NmQzODJhZjZiMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a","sha":"13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a"}],"sha":"fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/fe5fcf0828028ed8a2870876964276d382af6b2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:27:17Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:27:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: make the new-page spec configure its own site prerequisites (#28)\n\n03-new-page imported addSite and addSitemapMixin and called neither, relying\nentirely on 02-indexing having run first. That was harmless while indexation\ndegraded silently without them, and is not any more:\n\n  - the site must carry jmix:customGptIndexableSite or the registration gate\n    drops every operation;\n  - the site must have a usable sitemapIndexURL or resolvePublicUrl raises\n    instead of returning.\n\nRunning the spec alone would have failed on either, with a symptom that points\nnowhere near the cause. The spec''s own comment already warned about exactly this\nclass of coupling after a dryRun leak caused it once before.\n\nEvery mutation added here is idempotent, so the spec is now order-independent\neither way. Suite verified at 33/33 against Jahia 8.2.3.2 with the releases\nmanifest.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"9069edd9020c3ce95797ba24dbd39bb654757b18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/9069edd9020c3ce95797ba24dbd39bb654757b18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9069edd9020c3ce95797ba24dbd39bb654757b18\nparent 8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790792837 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790792837 +0200\n\ntest: make the new-page spec configure its own site prerequisites (#28)\n\n03-new-page imported addSite and addSitemapMixin and called neither, relying\nentirely on 02-indexing having run first. That was harmless while indexation\ndegraded silently without them, and is not any more:\n\n  - the site must carry jmix:customGptIndexableSite or the registration gate\n    drops every operation;\n  - the site must have a usable sitemapIndexURL or resolvePublicUrl raises\n    instead of returning.\n\nRunning the spec alone would have failed on either, with a symptom that points\nnowhere near the cause. The spec''s own comment already warned about exactly this\nclass of coupling after a dryRun leak caused it once before.\n\nEvery mutation added here is idempotent, so the spec is now order-independent\neither way. Suite verified at 33/33 against Jahia 8.2.3.2 with the releases\nmanifest.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVSFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU/EQAAgOH0jNt4LNKLDME1IJvH3n\nWSsX9ZTT1q5JPczaWaScAlpKK3NIeZ5HrOMhHVmUPlkkr27Io9XCoccDFCNfcL2P\ncaRqV1YrFesqJh6/u8Vo2DatVzFJZMW8ESx+Pc+pVDCtUTDPq5QCVRQ+9o+rMfJp\n8uPUzkYda5FcyO8RyGOpRyVnIoLatp/E8ZGVILTsB6dMq+TV+591q6idJLREgZ4+\nL96mucXP0AwfSHUXuLQCa8ZMJgluWAZo6CSykvMnhi2ISKzHLHVgF1Vv1C8v48Bl\nb2TtmaItGY2ctx1DCabGpRneFoUuGY1+pcizziQG5XJ73yyidljPePqmPuHin6ew\n7QXiBY5LbxDNfBLnAufhxdprSXoKq0WM070VK+PjpE8yjYjo2Ixz1ifx7jD6yGo3\nAPL0V5J1e6l7beLBlsfmjpUvGSWdoaC2Iem52phK6y+bXy+3VunA4ynszkJKL9MQ\ndbOssxZXit6ISoyDoYa48d0Bbzs+YUtIEMcvX6347to0mTWC/puMAyWrPJCusQ+R\nnnLPe4Et9+CWsblDSBGogW/iX8ddCRr+JfZH6EqbqxsPpCAPS7vrS2QqTOTT90L7\nVGYMFlJfLANNgMs6du1+mi/kb4BvSEHPbTU5l1mE6mDKSXT/WzwGTM/S+NBWHivX\nSez3ygyNnNxEf6NBsG7L\n=yLo/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:27:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDEzYmIzZjQ5YjJkZmY2ZDRkMzZlYWRmMzIyNTg4YjUxZGZhZGM0N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779","sha":"8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779"}],"sha":"13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/13bb3f49b2dff6d4d36eadf322588b51dfadc47a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:09:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:09:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: gate indexation on site registration, resolve vanity URLs, and verify the metadata write (#27)\n\n* fix: only index content from sites registered for CustomGPT\n\nacceptablePathToIndex checks the shape of a path and nothing else, so any\npublication anywhere under /sites/ produced an index operation whether or\nnot an administrator had registered the site with addSite. The site mixin\njmix:customGptIndexableSite was consulted when listing sites and nowhere on\nthe publish path.\n\nThis was measurable in production: a store.jahia.com page reached a corpus\nintended to hold one site''s content. A CustomGPT corpus cannot be filtered\nby origin, so it had to be identified and deleted by hand.\n\nAdd acceptableToIndex(path, indexer), the conjunction of the existing shape\ncheck and a new registration check, and call it from the four index-producing\nbranches of dispatchOperation. handleNodeRemove keeps bypassing the gate, as\nits comment already intended: removing a page that should not be in the corpus\nis always safe, and a delete is self-limiting because it is driven by a mapping\nnode that exists only for content this module indexed.\n\nThe gate fails closed. Failing to index a page that should have been indexed\nis repaired by the next publication or a re-index; indexing one that should\nnot have been contaminates a corpus with no way to filter by origin.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: bind the thread user for vanity URL resolution, and stop skipping a failed render silently\n\nTwo halves of the same production defect.\n\nJahia resolves vanity URLs inside rewriteOutbound through a JCR lookup that\nreads JCRSessionFactory.getCurrentUser(). Indexation runs on a pooled executor\nthread where the session is opened with doExecuteWithSystemSessionAsUser, which\nbinds the session''s user but not that thread-local. The lookup degraded to the\nraw .html path, Jahia answered it with a 302 to the vanity URL, and this module\ndeliberately does not follow redirects - so the page was never fetched.\n\nUtils.encode gains an overload that binds the user and restores the previous\nvalue in a finally. The restore matters: these threads are pooled and reused,\nso leaving a user bound would leak an identity into the next task.\n\nThe second half is why nobody saw it. indexJahiaPage logged ''Impossible to\nretrieve content from {}'' at WARN and returned, recording nothing, so the run\nstill reported success and the site was stamped as indexed over content that\nwas never uploaded. It now raises, and indexInSession records the failure it\nalready knows how to record.\n\nThis lands with the site-registration gate, not after it. On its own it would\nturn a silent failure into a silent contamination: pages from unregistered\nsites would start succeeding into a corpus that cannot be filtered by origin.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: verify the page metadata write, and repair pages indexed without a URL\n\nA 2xx on the metadata PUT is not evidence the write took. Under sustained bulk\nload this API answers status: success with an empty body while reporting zero\nerrors, and the write is dropped. 47 of 1920 pages in the production corpus\ncarry no URL because of it - 47 citations a user cannot click - and because the\nPUT ''succeeded'', nothing was ever logged.\n\nThe cause is not URL validation: version-range titles producing 170-character\npaths store fine, and the nulls track volume rather than content, with 36 of 47\nfrom a single high-volume day scattered across separate minutes.\n\nupdatePageMetadataChecked now reads the metadata back and retries until it\nmatches. It verifies data.id as well as data.url: a response that does not name\nthe page that was asked for is the exact signature measured at high concurrency,\nand comparing only the URL would accept another page''s metadata as proof.\n\nPageUrlRepair re-issues just the metadata write for pages that carry no URL.\nThe pages exist with correct content and their mapping nodes are intact, so\nthere is nothing to re-render or re-upload - one request per affected page\nrather than a full re-index. It walks mapping nodes rather than querying by\npage id, because customGptPageId is declared indexed=no. Exposed as the\nrepairPageUrls admin mutation, gated on customgpt-admin and site-admin.\n\nresolvePublicUrl is now shared by indexation and repair, so a repaired URL is\nby construction the URL indexation would have produced. That makes one\nbehaviour change: a site whose sitemapIndexURL is missing or malformed now\nrecords a failure instead of returning silently, which previously meant the\nsite indexed nothing at all and still reported success.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: also repair indexed pages whose stored URL is no longer canonical\n\nA stale URL is as user-visible as a missing one. 16 pages under\n/jahia-cloud/latest/ store a path that answers 301 to a different canonical\nURL, because ''latest'' is an alias segment in that tree; the redirect also\nnormalises case and spaces, so these are genuine vanity mappings rather than\ntrailing-slash noise. Every citation to them costs the reader a redirect.\n\nThe repair previously skipped any page whose url key was non-null, so all 16\nwere counted as intact. It now recomputes each page''s URL through\nresolvePublicUrl and rewrites whenever the stored value differs, which catches\nalias trees without having to enumerate which ones use aliases.\n\nMeasured scope, from a 150-page random sample of stored academy URLs requested\nwithout following redirects: 69.3% already canonical, 26.7% gated and not\nobservable anonymously, 3.3% dead, 0.7% redirecting. So this is a targeted case\nrather than a corpus-wide problem.\n\nSide effect worth having: readPage throws when the node is gone, so a page whose\ncontent no longer exists is now counted as failed and named in the log instead\nof passing silently as intact. Roughly 60 pages corpus-wide have a dead citation\nlink, including a security advisory. They need deleting from the corpus rather\nthan a rewritten URL, which is a separate remedy, but this at least surfaces\nthem.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"70fd1bba77a5da64ddd1e6d4d5d39a4855e32e7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/70fd1bba77a5da64ddd1e6d4d5d39a4855e32e7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779","verification":{"payload":"tree 70fd1bba77a5da64ddd1e6d4d5d39a4855e32e7e\nparent 3b1fe6409155dfecb5481e2af46a3d8393596d0d\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790791778 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790791778 +0200\n\nfix: gate indexation on site registration, resolve vanity URLs, and verify the metadata write (#27)\n\n* fix: only index content from sites registered for CustomGPT\n\nacceptablePathToIndex checks the shape of a path and nothing else, so any\npublication anywhere under /sites/ produced an index operation whether or\nnot an administrator had registered the site with addSite. The site mixin\njmix:customGptIndexableSite was consulted when listing sites and nowhere on\nthe publish path.\n\nThis was measurable in production: a store.jahia.com page reached a corpus\nintended to hold one site''s content. A CustomGPT corpus cannot be filtered\nby origin, so it had to be identified and deleted by hand.\n\nAdd acceptableToIndex(path, indexer), the conjunction of the existing shape\ncheck and a new registration check, and call it from the four index-producing\nbranches of dispatchOperation. handleNodeRemove keeps bypassing the gate, as\nits comment already intended: removing a page that should not be in the corpus\nis always safe, and a delete is self-limiting because it is driven by a mapping\nnode that exists only for content this module indexed.\n\nThe gate fails closed. Failing to index a page that should have been indexed\nis repaired by the next publication or a re-index; indexing one that should\nnot have been contaminates a corpus with no way to filter by origin.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: bind the thread user for vanity URL resolution, and stop skipping a failed render silently\n\nTwo halves of the same production defect.\n\nJahia resolves vanity URLs inside rewriteOutbound through a JCR lookup that\nreads JCRSessionFactory.getCurrentUser(). Indexation runs on a pooled executor\nthread where the session is opened with doExecuteWithSystemSessionAsUser, which\nbinds the session''s user but not that thread-local. The lookup degraded to the\nraw .html path, Jahia answered it with a 302 to the vanity URL, and this module\ndeliberately does not follow redirects - so the page was never fetched.\n\nUtils.encode gains an overload that binds the user and restores the previous\nvalue in a finally. The restore matters: these threads are pooled and reused,\nso leaving a user bound would leak an identity into the next task.\n\nThe second half is why nobody saw it. indexJahiaPage logged ''Impossible to\nretrieve content from {}'' at WARN and returned, recording nothing, so the run\nstill reported success and the site was stamped as indexed over content that\nwas never uploaded. It now raises, and indexInSession records the failure it\nalready knows how to record.\n\nThis lands with the site-registration gate, not after it. On its own it would\nturn a silent failure into a silent contamination: pages from unregistered\nsites would start succeeding into a corpus that cannot be filtered by origin.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: verify the page metadata write, and repair pages indexed without a URL\n\nA 2xx on the metadata PUT is not evidence the write took. Under sustained bulk\nload this API answers status: success with an empty body while reporting zero\nerrors, and the write is dropped. 47 of 1920 pages in the production corpus\ncarry no URL because of it - 47 citations a user cannot click - and because the\nPUT ''succeeded'', nothing was ever logged.\n\nThe cause is not URL validation: version-range titles producing 170-character\npaths store fine, and the nulls track volume rather than content, with 36 of 47\nfrom a single high-volume day scattered across separate minutes.\n\nupdatePageMetadataChecked now reads the metadata back and retries until it\nmatches. It verifies data.id as well as data.url: a response that does not name\nthe page that was asked for is the exact signature measured at high concurrency,\nand comparing only the URL would accept another page''s metadata as proof.\n\nPageUrlRepair re-issues just the metadata write for pages that carry no URL.\nThe pages exist with correct content and their mapping nodes are intact, so\nthere is nothing to re-render or re-upload - one request per affected page\nrather than a full re-index. It walks mapping nodes rather than querying by\npage id, because customGptPageId is declared indexed=no. Exposed as the\nrepairPageUrls admin mutation, gated on customgpt-admin and site-admin.\n\nresolvePublicUrl is now shared by indexation and repair, so a repaired URL is\nby construction the URL indexation would have produced. That makes one\nbehaviour change: a site whose sitemapIndexURL is missing or malformed now\nrecords a failure instead of returning silently, which previously meant the\nsite indexed nothing at all and still reported success.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: also repair indexed pages whose stored URL is no longer canonical\n\nA stale URL is as user-visible as a missing one. 16 pages under\n/jahia-cloud/latest/ store a path that answers 301 to a different canonical\nURL, because ''latest'' is an alias segment in that tree; the redirect also\nnormalises case and spaces, so these are genuine vanity mappings rather than\ntrailing-slash noise. Every citation to them costs the reader a redirect.\n\nThe repair previously skipped any page whose url key was non-null, so all 16\nwere counted as intact. It now recomputes each page''s URL through\nresolvePublicUrl and rewrites whenever the stored value differs, which catches\nalias trees without having to enumerate which ones use aliases.\n\nMeasured scope, from a 150-page random sample of stored academy URLs requested\nwithout following redirects: 69.3% already canonical, 26.7% gated and not\nobservable anonymously, 3.3% dead, 0.7% redirecting. So this is a targeted case\nrather than a corpus-wide problem.\n\nSide effect worth having: readPage throws when the node is gone, so a page whose\ncontent no longer exists is now counted as failed and named in the log instead\nof passing silently as intact. Roughly 60 pages corpus-wide have a dead citation\nlink, including a security advisory. They need deleting from the corpus rather\nthan a rewritten URL, which is a separate remedy, but this at least surfaces\nthem.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVBiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuSkQAAAcrWbgmT3dgOwnKv6YZOmg\nJckJe/wxHQFiyj5/7HMr8Uuo3+TGwXHHUBc3OVCX7mLpvAjXsBVe0BM3ayDP+/oN\nm6wPTyn2SdztTROgQNDn0VEPECZ0UAlokDvNAZuKR4QljqdEpJB4UShQgx9cjrgj\nR1EF0uD0eqxnUKxNUQuvyEa0pBH78tVVL1+DyYhoh1XigyAG3Wgsu1bCdn4nQOTe\nk4NVZ/KsqCcKUs1j3kRTPmyA7brr3/6wy54U14Brr7x88xMlaPslsrVuxePrZwQD\n1kMGDsiCVV5Yh8HwdGF+ZRXGppXJLbXYJFOIUZicyP3TeQcHhe2YSoiOso7pSke7\nog1e61s+R5hhwv1OIDKNLIg2mA2ONUn+tMF03cRcIhK1M0DJea14ZEIZBo4lC5LA\nzHaeT4w5H4jWZPU7ubGMfT9PEb+RhJ++UYJUi+gAHTu5cx2CaRrNGb9Qf5v+qrFS\nCBqYhU+D7hclwjTuQl0B8kNa6KybiggGz/uDHEGmsmXp1RahM9/rP+9i9kFAufnP\nLklVm0HzI6KwC83IDJ/mxTsiJMVP/qlbK1e+CkUxHN+aTOkwsgPd3+tmRRfUDKXl\ntWEpQYGWMn+XJS1obw6nWcok+emnrPheHXtLP2PTEIgZFDepltBZ+W32OwRAnic0\n5ps9iPkKVsUsf6spFI+9\n=wZBi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:09:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/8ba4ef6968d64c441f8ef3cc2aa20914e348c779","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDhiYTRlZjY5NjhkNjRjNDQxZjhlZjNjYzJhYTIwOTE0ZTM0OGM3Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"ht