gin, which would also deploy to Nexus.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"32a75b4ea8540d8ec6f4838ba5978008e2f23078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/32a75b4ea8540d8ec6f4838ba5978008e2f23078"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/7bd82f4972b44d574d2ceccba7d6946b46c47e54","verification":{"payload":"tree 32a75b4ea8540d8ec6f4838ba5978008e2f23078\nparent 8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790769157 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790769157 +0200\n\nchore: set version to 1.0.7 for release\n\nDone by hand rather than via maven-release-plugin, which would also deploy to Nexus.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmq8+AUACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mX6Qf9HK2tyw6K5Rv+rWFOOgtXrCkw5+joNihAosFBxSRNYD9YCRR0wVHhtCwI\nG7Y70X7XK/m+jlbop7feqiykO8pYwv7GXNl9lLiMhnD94Lm7U0Sk8wWJX5Ya3rO+\nJZfUSNnuOprnPfMjX5HjSKP9x0dg4hFOsKVIXHEOt34rNq2sTrDZdpHGlrqAIABv\nDF8GZnx1a3sTA/njJgdhPsCGDJoIPM8XJ90qAlMsiq6VahKho+ag0SfFQGaU/3dR\nRGPtXB8mjB65Wjpb6FaMVaYrk8Ul36zpJq8W05N46pNRyNj2sbDiuhknghI+CxiB\nH/Z7d72JzirI6UpdFxfG7/lj+g9ljQ==\n=kWk5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:52:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/7bd82f4972b44d574d2ceccba7d6946b46c47e54","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDdiZDgyZjQ5NzJiNDRkNTc0ZDJjZWNjYmE3ZDY5NDZiNDZjNDdlNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e","sha":"8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e"}],"sha":"7bd82f4972b44d574d2ceccba7d6946b46c47e54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/7bd82f4972b44d574d2ceccba7d6946b46c47e54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:44:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:44:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: stop a failed CustomGPT delete from orphaning a page, and coalesce repeat index operations (#26)\n\nA corpus audit of the academy CustomGPT project found 223 of 3055 pages\nredundant, concentrated in the security-advisory tree, with one URL holding\n17 copies. Superseded copies of advisories stayed retrievable, so the chatbot\ncould answer from a withdrawn one.\n\nCause: removeExistingPage() discarded the boolean returned by\ndeleteCustomGptPage(), then added a replacement unconditionally. Every\nre-publish whose DELETE failed left the previous page in the project, with no\nlog line at any level.\n\ndeleteCustomGptPage() now reports the HTTP status rather than a boolean, and\nlogs status and body on any non-2xx. removeExistingPage() acts on it:\n\n  2xx  the page is gone; proceed\n  403  the page was already gone; proceed\n  else the page may still be there; abort WITHOUT adding a replacement\n\nThe 403 case is measured, not assumed. This API answers\n403 {\"message\": \"This action is unauthorized.\"} for a page id that no longer\nexists, rather than 404 - consistently across 48 requests. A stale id in the\nsidecar is the ordinary case and leaves nothing behind, so treating 404 as\n\"gone\" (the obvious choice) would have aborted on every stale id and stalled\nre-indexing entirely. Aborting on the remaining statuses leaves content stale\nuntil the next publication, which is recoverable; a duplicate is not, short of\nan out-of-band purge.\n\nAlso coalesces repeat operations. One publication is not one JCR save:\nJCRPublicationService.publish saves repeatedly across the subtree, each save\ndelivers its own event batch, and IndexerJCRListener.onEvent builds a fresh\nIndexOperations per batch - so its de-duplication cannot see across batches\nand the same node was dispatched up to 10 times for one publication, a few\nseconds apart. Correctness never depended on this: with a working DELETE the\nrepeats converge on one page regardless. The cost did - N deletes and N posts\nto reach a state one of each would reach, against an API that degrades under\nsustained volume, so the redundant calls consume the budget whose exhaustion\ncauses the degradation.\n\nproduceAsynchronousOperations now claims each operation''s node and drops\nrepeats while equivalent work is queued or running, releasing on completion.\nType is part of the key, so a removal is not coalesced against an indexation.\nThe trade-off, documented at the method: a genuine second change published\nwhile the first index is still pending is dropped rather than queued, so that\ncontent waits for the next publication.\n\nLogged at INFO rather than DEBUG. This drops indexing work, and the symptom of\na wrong key would be content silently not indexed - the same shape as the\ndefects fixed in #25, where a consequential decision left no evidence.\n\nTests: 157. Six mutations fail the suite - discarding the delete status (the\noriginal bug), treating 403 as failure, treating any status as gone, removing\ncoalescing, never releasing a key, and dropping type from the key. An earlier\nversion of the delete tests pinned only the status classification and left the\noriginal bug surviving; removeExistingPage is now exercised directly.\n\nVerified on Jahia 8.2.3.2 with credentials, All specs passed 33/33 on both\nchanges. A real DELETE returned 403 during the run and was correctly treated\nas gone, with zero false aborts; coalescing engaged twice, each time dropping\na whole redundant batch.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"369511bec0668f17cabacdbce6c089fabe25e369","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/369511bec0668f17cabacdbce6c089fabe25e369"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e","verification":{"payload":"tree 369511bec0668f17cabacdbce6c089fabe25e369\nparent 6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790768663 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790768663 +0200\n\nfix: stop a failed CustomGPT delete from orphaning a page, and coalesce repeat index operations (#26)\n\nA corpus audit of the academy CustomGPT project found 223 of 3055 pages\nredundant, concentrated in the security-advisory tree, with one URL holding\n17 copies. Superseded copies of advisories stayed retrievable, so the chatbot\ncould answer from a withdrawn one.\n\nCause: removeExistingPage() discarded the boolean returned by\ndeleteCustomGptPage(), then added a replacement unconditionally. Every\nre-publish whose DELETE failed left the previous page in the project, with no\nlog line at any level.\n\ndeleteCustomGptPage() now reports the HTTP status rather than a boolean, and\nlogs status and body on any non-2xx. removeExistingPage() acts on it:\n\n  2xx  the page is gone; proceed\n  403  the page was already gone; proceed\n  else the page may still be there; abort WITHOUT adding a replacement\n\nThe 403 case is measured, not assumed. This API answers\n403 {\"message\": \"This action is unauthorized.\"} for a page id that no longer\nexists, rather than 404 - consistently across 48 requests. A stale id in the\nsidecar is the ordinary case and leaves nothing behind, so treating 404 as\n\"gone\" (the obvious choice) would have aborted on every stale id and stalled\nre-indexing entirely. Aborting on the remaining statuses leaves content stale\nuntil the next publication, which is recoverable; a duplicate is not, short of\nan out-of-band purge.\n\nAlso coalesces repeat operations. One publication is not one JCR save:\nJCRPublicationService.publish saves repeatedly across the subtree, each save\ndelivers its own event batch, and IndexerJCRListener.onEvent builds a fresh\nIndexOperations per batch - so its de-duplication cannot see across batches\nand the same node was dispatched up to 10 times for one publication, a few\nseconds apart. Correctness never depended on this: with a working DELETE the\nrepeats converge on one page regardless. The cost did - N deletes and N posts\nto reach a state one of each would reach, against an API that degrades under\nsustained volume, so the redundant calls consume the budget whose exhaustion\ncauses the degradation.\n\nproduceAsynchronousOperations now claims each operation''s node and drops\nrepeats while equivalent work is queued or running, releasing on completion.\nType is part of the key, so a removal is not coalesced against an indexation.\nThe trade-off, documented at the method: a genuine second change published\nwhile the first index is still pending is dropped rather than queued, so that\ncontent waits for the next publication.\n\nLogged at INFO rather than DEBUG. This drops indexing work, and the symptom of\na wrong key would be content silently not indexed - the same shape as the\ndefects fixed in #25, where a consequential decision left no evidence.\n\nTests: 157. Six mutations fail the suite - discarding the delete status (the\noriginal bug), treating 403 as failure, treating any status as gone, removing\ncoalescing, never releasing a key, and dropping type from the key. An earlier\nversion of the delete tests pinned only the status classification and left the\noriginal bug surviving; removeExistingPage is now exercised directly.\n\nVerified on Jahia 8.2.3.2 with credentials, All specs passed 33/33 on both\nchanges. A real DELETE returned 403 during the run and was correctly treated\nas gone, with zero false aborts; coalescing engaged twice, each time dropping\na whole redundant batch.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPYXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxWEQAEaupNPEmANGLuxYAq9hBVm6\nRitNWp9qz6uKWoTU1vzuPv+SiYdjWbJPFIMb+kNVo8jZF5bNSlZmZzHXHsjeETkE\nQ4Vb3XQ4dOS41W2bSbbGF5XLbbXirJT/HL+xWl8MWa//1/9sxBS46rZf7QDyJ7pf\nQkViZ3jF8kOKhyM3XuRpL6py7VxSA3hlASfA00gY9k3mkurscbOQqB8g4wD3Mm58\n2T79zRXu/7b77GnXR0IdcwJwajnWh4l68HRQv0sMrKXjZ5/NCmdtfsHackTCaZ/m\nk/vB2tf0ldBu9+uK8sKKNbVkO38+0x0OuGWuXU6OiiHvFVAfkm0SzbgJ/1H74qeW\nV7WarD83BbAo2YvXRv53sSqOLYhtbDbd8yWStTfboIQPGIskAaJTJHU/iMhnl/vb\nci/8yrUVPXISc62/anoLzSYRJCVuw8cJig//uhAGAn1MSoXVm3V5vCJeQLI83mBC\nDalr1eKje4Qh0Krj7ePOFrksI2ShmA/Jii4U5QdBreYlviaIyVkDs+qzH0TaZsJT\n58M+ZadY3GJmd5GmBnGUwcSKbPkrht8o/YWpjPYQ+jkkLI62PrKUaXltVD6rLHAc\nOIJtXY2XOhBpIAxcTgUeqdH/Esdxdn+zTLKziwygGa0PvB8Uc1PQWJq6yL7cNfeX\nhS+kZtkB0pinb0U4wG4i\n=yGW3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:44:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDhiZTk2NDg0M2RiNjBjYjc4NTRkNjEwM2JkNDBmMDdkMjk1MTg4OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63","sha":"6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63"}],"sha":"8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/8be964843db60cb7854d6103bd40f07d2951889e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:16:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:16:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: deaf listener, silently-successful failed indexation, and dry-run opacity (#25)\n\nFollow-ups to #23. Each of the three was more than the reported symptom.\n\n1. A listener with an empty node-type filter was registered and silently\n   deaf. getNodeTypes() resolved its filter live on every call, and Jahia\n   re-invokes it when registering, independently of any check the caller\n   makes - so an earlier attempt at this was a TOCTOU and was reverted. The\n   listener now resolves its filter once in its constructor, making the\n   checked array the registered array. registerJcrListeners() refuses an\n   empty filter, since checkNodeTypeNames rejects every event against one:\n   such a listener is registered, reported healthy, and receives nothing for\n   the life of the component. refreshJcrListeners() recovers on the next\n   configuration update, and also re-registers when the indexed node types\n   change - that filter was previously frozen at first registration.\n\n2. A failed site indexation reported COMPLETED. Three layers, and the first\n   two alone would have looked like a fix while changing nothing: the\n   supplier swallowed every failure so whenCompleteAsync''s throwable was\n   always null; status derives from indexationInProgress rather than the end\n   timestamp, so withholding the timestamp would have left sites stuck\n   showing STARTED; and the dominant case was a per-node swallow further\n   down, which the e2e exposed as 9 failures with 0 propagated. Per-node\n   failures are now recorded on the Indexer with node path and language,\n   indexAllOperations raises if any node failed, and a failure marker plus a\n   FAILED status carry the outcome without making the site look hung.\n\n3. customgptIndex not appearing after a publish - neither a module bug nor\n   the spec''s timeout. cy.waitUntil already allowed 60s, but its predicate\n   read result.data.jcr with optional chaining starting too late, so an\n   errored query made it throw TypeError and abort in 11s without using its\n   budget. Fixing that exposed the real cause: 02-indexing''s after() hook\n   resets dryRun to true, 03-new-page set no settings of its own, and\n   indexInSession returned silently on dry run. That matters beyond the test\n   - dryRun defaults to true in the shipped .cfg, which is marked\n   won''t-be-overridden, so this silent return is the likeliest reason for\n   \"the module runs but nothing is indexed\" on a real install.\n\nThe metadata-update failure now carries the response body, which identified\nthe e2e''s 422s as environmental (CustomGPT rejects the internal docker\nhostname) rather than a defect.\n\n147 unit tests. Mutation-checked: reverting the deaf-listener refusal fails\n2 tests, making the outcome handler ignore its throwable fails 1. Cypress\ne2e on Jahia 8.2.3.2 with credentials: All specs passed, 33/33 - the first\nfully green run - and verified to pass for the right reasons rather than on\nthe tally alone.\n\nNOT addressed here: per-language duplication of the production corpus. A\npeer audit measured 993 of 3055 pages (32%) redundant. The sidecar is keyed\nby node path while index requests are created per language, so it retains\nonly the last language''s page id and each republish orphans the rest.\nCorpus evidence (41/41 same-second groups at identical filesize) shows the\nper-language renders are byte-identical for untranslated pages, so a correct\nfix needs render de-duplication, not just per-language keying. Tracked for a\nseparate change; superseded security advisories stay retrievable until then.","tree":{"sha":"1b3fbcadcdf0d316812c839cfb3041b6e087b6d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/1b3fbcadcdf0d316812c839cfb3041b6e087b6d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b3fbcadcdf0d316812c839cfb3041b6e087b6d7\nparent 2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790759790 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790759790 +0200\n\nfix: deaf listener, silently-successful failed indexation, and dry-run opacity (#25)\n\nFollow-ups to #23. Each of the three was more than the reported symptom.\n\n1. A listener with an empty node-type filter was registered and silently\n   deaf. getNodeTypes() resolved its filter live on every call, and Jahia\n   re-invokes it when registering, independently of any check the caller\n   makes - so an earlier attempt at this was a TOCTOU and was reverted. The\n   listener now resolves its filter once in its constructor, making the\n   checked array the registered array. registerJcrListeners() refuses an\n   empty filter, since checkNodeTypeNames rejects every event against one:\n   such a listener is registered, reported healthy, and receives nothing for\n   the life of the component. refreshJcrListeners() recovers on the next\n   configuration update, and also re-registers when the indexed node types\n   change - that filter was previously frozen at first registration.\n\n2. A failed site indexation reported COMPLETED. Three layers, and the first\n   two alone would have looked like a fix while changing nothing: the\n   supplier swallowed every failure so whenCompleteAsync''s throwable was\n   always null; status derives from indexationInProgress rather than the end\n   timestamp, so withholding the timestamp would have left sites stuck\n   showing STARTED; and the dominant case was a per-node swallow further\n   down, which the e2e exposed as 9 failures with 0 propagated. Per-node\n   failures are now recorded on the Indexer with node path and language,\n   indexAllOperations raises if any node failed, and a failure marker plus a\n   FAILED status carry the outcome without making the site look hung.\n\n3. customgptIndex not appearing after a publish - neither a module bug nor\n   the spec''s timeout. cy.waitUntil already allowed 60s, but its predicate\n   read result.data.jcr with optional chaining starting too late, so an\n   errored query made it throw TypeError and abort in 11s without using its\n   budget. Fixing that exposed the real cause: 02-indexing''s after() hook\n   resets dryRun to true, 03-new-page set no settings of its own, and\n   indexInSession returned silently on dry run. That matters beyond the test\n   - dryRun defaults to true in the shipped .cfg, which is marked\n   won''t-be-overridden, so this silent return is the likeliest reason for\n   \"the module runs but nothing is indexed\" on a real install.\n\nThe metadata-update failure now carries the response body, which identified\nthe e2e''s 422s as environmental (CustomGPT rejects the internal docker\nhostname) rather than a defect.\n\n147 unit tests. Mutation-checked: reverting the deaf-listener refusal fails\n2 tests, making the outcome handler ignore its throwable fails 1. Cypress\ne2e on Jahia 8.2.3.2 with credentials: All specs passed, 33/33 - the first\nfully green run - and verified to pass for the right reasons rather than on\nthe tally alone.\n\nNOT addressed here: per-language duplication of the production corpus. A\npeer audit measured 993 of 3055 pages (32%) redundant. The sidecar is keyed\nby node path while index requests are created per language, so it retains\nonly the last language''s page id and each republish orphans the rest.\nCorpus evidence (41/41 same-second groups at identical filesize) shows the\nper-language renders are byte-identical for untranslated pages, so a correct\nfix needs render de-duplication, not just per-language keying. Tracked for a\nseparate change; superseded security advisories stay retrievable until then.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvNNuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiVQQAEAStlA1C+tFW29rcateN676\nPkXlgDd/GHzaQRmbEqtv/NZ7mqICR0GCGLwiaaojWJwgl0Zb8cjDcSKZGpLnBbXv\nYSIVEinhy0GX2aIlm8hzeqlHzMYPs7qzXv3eXyPuVvFyIXpk5S78AGgjTYih2uEl\nWP78MXhwPQAvB2LwLzn3R0qn4U1Cvu2GVCqTYuCXr3Xgk/NZleKHZ4vbhiHITmA1\nq4dwolDMdGzWIYQYbT7lFTWBrwDNEradj4lJO9agnzo3aHUqzf4y4QAiHdZwDre0\nmSMKkyRkxbSsbe2cgh52xNWYfrX7Mbjwk8NYgRNiDMu5OHPkLCMY/Uu0o8LyS7zW\nGhkmNnbfIOAhBjyvifco+5O3RbWOqUprqqMk11nF3/rtsimVzA3Z/auWoA/g54y4\ngwGZmyGMGFmzDwGO7PrHJBO8LgPCjNsSqQW3oLgndwaWQl64qGvxoa6T5B4oRMK4\nlDuwFW5ZX4ti9pCAlKG2gzfpvFspnY+iL2oW/4zNPPn1Z0+Vm4MEg/z28RRhsQrK\ngXhtfb0fCgjUjXL2Fh7pY+MeJy4OWEnS3h/MLOAmkcQQl4Y/qo9ThV/nndLtmx77\nNZq5RekWhsuHFqRB1/VqzO4fGITIX1Z1fcIO4pIwdPHoSHYzLUHORTEUdxq7SaQy\nrQcEWcGL0E6CzmPcSc8e\n=VF3R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T09:16:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDZmYmQyMDhhMTgxOGEzOTk3MmVlYzRiODcxNWM2YmQzYmE1YjVjNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c","sha":"2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c"}],"sha":"6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/6fbd208a1818a39972eec4b8715c6bd3ba5b5c63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:36:54Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:36:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: prevent the JCR listener from outliving its bundle (JAHIACOM-1675) (#23)\n\nA publication failed with NoClassDefFoundError on\nIndexOperations$CustomGptOperationType, thrown by an IndexerJCRListener that\nhad outlived the bundle classloader which created it. A wiring refresh did\nnot help; only restarting the processing node did.\n\nVerified against decompiled jahia-impl-8.2.3.2: JCRObservationManager keeps\nlisteners in a JVM-wide static list and removes them by instance identity,\nwhile TemplatePackageRegistry de-duplicates by Class identity. A listener\nthat stop() fails to detach is therefore unreachable forever - a redeploy\nregisters a second listener beside the stale one rather than replacing it.\nJCRObservationManager.consume wraps listeners in catch (Exception) but not\nError, which is why a NoClassDefFoundError killed the PublicationJob while\nordinary exceptions never did.\n\nModule changes:\n- stop() latches a terminal `disposed` flag, withdraws the EventHandler\n  registration, then detaches the listener unconditionally; every step is\n  isolated by runQuietly, which catches RuntimeException and LinkageError.\n- init() registers the listener LAST, after everything that can throw. A\n  component whose activate() throws is never deactivated (OSGi Compendium\n  112.5.8), so registering first stranded the listener on a path no amount\n  of stop() hardening could reach.\n- handleEvent() refuses events once disposed; EventAdmin delivery is not\n  transactional, so it could otherwise schedule a Quartz job belonging to\n  the bundle being torn down.\n- onEvent() contains RuntimeException and LinkageError so a stale listener\n  can no longer abort an unrelated publication.\n- restartExecutor* refuses to allocate a pool once disposed.\n- The HTTP clients are closed once from stop(), after every pool, never\n  from the per-pool helper, which also runs during normal operation on a\n  caller-local pool. The shutdown budget is 60s, deliberately no shorter\n  than one call timeout: indexing a node is a DELETE followed by a re-add,\n  so a worker interrupted mid-sequence removes a page from the customer''s\n  CustomGPT project without recreating it.\n- pom.xml stops exporting indexer.listener (hygiene; it was not the cause).\n\nTest harness: the Cypress suite had been failing 20 of 33 for a harness\nreason - Jahia auto-installs Jahia-Depends at LATEST, which against a\nsnapshot-carrying repository group resolved serverSettings to a SNAPSHOT\nrequiring a newer Jahia, whereupon Jahia stopped the working serverSettings\nto make way for it and the admin UI went down. The new manifest replaces the\nrepository list with releases-only jahia-releases, and .env.example pins a\nreleased Jahia.\n\nVerification: 141 unit tests; four regressions that previously survived the\nsuite now fail it. Cypress on Jahia 8.2.3.2 with credentials: 33 tests, 31\npassing, 2 failing - the 2 are pre-existing, matching a main baseline run\nbyte for byte, and are tracked as follow-ups along with the deaf-listener\nbug and the cancelled-indexation-reported-COMPLETE bug.\n\nNOTE: deploying this does not remediate an already-stranded node. The stale\ninstance belongs to the previous class and has no LinkageError handler; such\nnodes still need a restart.","tree":{"sha":"3b6c2aed3efa4cb94861a988051997ac8150bb4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/3b6c2aed3efa4cb94861a988051997ac8150bb4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b6c2aed3efa4cb94861a988051997ac8150bb4c\nparent 2d6475450e70c8f81078a792c744d0ad3eb49450\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1790757414 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790757414 +0200\n\nfix: prevent the JCR listener from outliving its bundle (JAHIACOM-1675) (#23)\n\nA publication failed with NoClassDefFoundError on\nIndexOperations$CustomGptOperationType, thrown by an IndexerJCRListener that\nhad outlived the bundle classloader which created it. A wiring refresh did\nnot help; only restarting the processing node did.\n\nVerified against decompiled jahia-impl-8.2.3.2: JCRObservationManager keeps\nlisteners in a JVM-wide static list and removes them by instance identity,\nwhile TemplatePackageRegistry de-duplicates by Class identity. A listener\nthat stop() fails to detach is therefore unreachable forever - a redeploy\nregisters a second listener beside the stale one rather than replacing it.\nJCRObservationManager.consume wraps listeners in catch (Exception) but not\nError, which is why a NoClassDefFoundError killed the PublicationJob while\nordinary exceptions never did.\n\nModule changes:\n- stop() latches a terminal `disposed` flag, withdraws the EventHandler\n  registration, then detaches the listener unconditionally; every step is\n  isolated by runQuietly, which catches RuntimeException and LinkageError.\n- init() registers the listener LAST, after everything that can throw. A\n  component whose activate() throws is never deactivated (OSGi Compendium\n  112.5.8), so registering first stranded the listener on a path no amount\n  of stop() hardening could reach.\n- handleEvent() refuses events once disposed; EventAdmin delivery is not\n  transactional, so it could otherwise schedule a Quartz job belonging to\n  the bundle being torn down.\n- onEvent() contains RuntimeException and LinkageError so a stale listener\n  can no longer abort an unrelated publication.\n- restartExecutor* refuses to allocate a pool once disposed.\n- The HTTP clients are closed once from stop(), after every pool, never\n  from the per-pool helper, which also runs during normal operation on a\n  caller-local pool. The shutdown budget is 60s, deliberately no shorter\n  than one call timeout: indexing a node is a DELETE followed by a re-add,\n  so a worker interrupted mid-sequence removes a page from the customer''s\n  CustomGPT project without recreating it.\n- pom.xml stops exporting indexer.listener (hygiene; it was not the cause).\n\nTest harness: the Cypress suite had been failing 20 of 33 for a harness\nreason - Jahia auto-installs Jahia-Depends at LATEST, which against a\nsnapshot-carrying repository group resolved serverSettings to a SNAPSHOT\nrequiring a newer Jahia, whereupon Jahia stopped the working serverSettings\nto make way for it and the admin UI went down. The new manifest replaces the\nrepository list with releases-only jahia-releases, and .env.example pins a\nreleased Jahia.\n\nVerification: 141 unit tests; four regressions that previously survived the\nsuite now fail it. Cypress on Jahia 8.2.3.2 with credentials: 33 tests, 31\npassing, 2 failing - the 2 are pre-existing, matching a main baseline run\nbyte for byte, and are tracked as follow-ups along with the deaf-listener\nbug and the cancelled-indexation-reported-COMPLETE bug.\n\nNOTE: deploying this does not remediate an already-stranded node. The stale\ninstance belongs to the previous class and has no LinkageError handler; such\nnodes still need a restart.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMomCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3TQQAJsUWO0bm05hmh/lKtmkLhHc\nJJS24WzOCGH+cZecgYB50aYngcqkhSvlP8Cu3iMKp5uADq0iMjTWZYSXgKV6sOQ3\nj6NivAHE1Yjhg7nNKdIbk2ICWuSNRUQOXn/aRZfKeWWtkmv9M0mmsZ/I5FPYm2xd\n/ZuyzOOJSIhsK5F3g5/R0ac8jDJsgcLENBRJkMW06jwrYx7eltyGUrW+1DDdtTkx\n4rFQDkhSFw60za7mM22teACpOJKQKNgdj7lvg4N6ZyYBz4nGc29kJVPFMiX2KS74\nYnoRpSs7njmthn6iH+9MnEWlCBHHmepbCl8Qu1GvrmCZSQZd25ZWSNzl/5CP9ZxJ\nx8H4alSL4yqxwz1mbC+RslfbFp9ZW3PNuapKm6FTkJn5tdIb0QdSQ8ywgK82hU1c\n5ebSQusmvP516OrpdxqCPDoaAiA5ZyKZ0LSK9kXvJ9Vuxik8SdjseHrzupTG9/z4\nJ/uYWtwxWJC3EITJrQjDC68sNlkw9goToZLg4xi0/RGltDairaGGtsVtEcQeoeLy\nCHPdAMQV6jKtSmk9HVUtjtWTAqhrPNd/Hf5k4cpc6W4JhPugh2oVl3Qb+AQROA42\nAMwEk5e+vFLmgpAcbjay8yeaw7qjFw15gxT6tedA0RM2yTfuChbz9pc/6sI14Y0v\nCG7HyTFdpW2UxKf3406U\n=R5LE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:36:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDJkMDc3NWYzODM1OTNlZDM0M2JlMmVjZjJmYjQ2YjA2MjQzMGVhNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/2d6475450e70c8f81078a792c744d0ad3eb49450","sha":"2d6475450e70c8f81078a792c744d0ad3eb49450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2d6475450e70c8f81078a792c744d0ad3eb49450"}],"sha":"2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2d0775f383593ed343be2ecf2fb46b062430ea5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/2d6475450e70c8f81078a792c744d0ad3eb49450/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:01:28Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:01:28Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"chore: enable dependabot version update