ml_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450","sha":"86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450"}],"sha":"fa7bc950a31466adf29299024e879a9035456d81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/fa7bc950a31466adf29299024e879a9035456d81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T19:28:00Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T19:28:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: harden customgpt-ai (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests) (#7)\n\n* chore: harden customgpt-ai (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests)\n\nBlind multi-level review (architecture, security, code quality, ergonomy,\naccessibility AAA, test coverage, documentation) and remediation.\n\nSecurity\n- SSRF guard: reject private/loopback/link-local/unique-local IP literals\n  for the CustomGPT API base URL and the page-render host (no DNS of\n  arbitrary hostnames); validate base URL is https in Config so bad .cfg\n  values cannot reach the HTTP layer carrying the Bearer token.\n- Explicit OkHttp connect/read/write/call timeouts on both clients.\n- GraphQL resolvers no longer leak internal exception detail to clients\n  (server-side log + generic message); audit-log admin actions\n  (saveSettings/startIndex/startNodeIndex/addSite/purgeAllPages) with the\n  sanitized acting user; validate addSite siteKey against ^[\\w-]+$.\n\nCorrectness / quality (Java)\n- Fix CustomGptIndexOperation equals/hashCode field-set mismatch that\n  corrupted LinkedHashSet de-duplication.\n- Thread-safety: volatile + synchronized executor restart, synchronized\n  init(); narrow broad catch(Exception); fix JCR event-type bit test\n  ((type & PROPERTY_EVENTS) != 0); remove dead code (duplicate ACE branch,\n  nodeToReindex map, write-only retryOnConflict, vacuous null guards);\n  hasProperty guard; lambdas for SAM callbacks; rename misspelled constants.\n\nFrontend / ergonomy\n- Remove console logging; one-time form init (drop Apollo onCompleted reset);\n  NaN guard + min/max on numeric inputs; client-side required-field\n  validation; name the GraphQL query and route/init functions.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA)\n- Native <output> polite live regions (deduped), dialog focus return,\n  aria-describedby hints, aria-invalid + inline errors, 24px touch targets,\n  AAA contrast, <form> semantics, prefers-reduced-motion, i18n parity (de/fr).\n\nTests\n- 22 -> 117 Java unit tests (RateLimitInterceptor, Indexer dedup, Config\n  parse, Service path predicate, SSRF guard) + 16 Jest/RTL tests.\n- Cypress: self-contained masking round-trip test, replace cy.wait(10000)\n  with polling, restore teardown, add saveSettings/purgeAllPages permission\n  deny tests.\n\nBuild / docs\n- Sync package.json version to pom (1.0.7-SNAPSHOT); add SonarQube\n  properties; correct AGENTS.md (React 18, pure OSGi DS).\n\nSonarQube quality gate: OK (0 new issues, ratings A, 0% duplication).\nCypress: 29 passing / 0 failing / 4 skipped (indexing specs need live creds).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review (SSRF dotless-IP bypass, double-submit, focus, landmark)\n\nBlind PR review findings:\n- Security (HIGH): SSRF guard bypass via dotless integer/decimal IPv4\n  literals (e.g. https://2130706433 -> 127.0.0.1, https://0 -> 0.0.0.0)\n  passed isHttpsUrl/isInternalHost because isIpLiteral required a dot.\n  Classify all-digit dotless values as IP literals so they are resolved\n  and range-checked; add tests. (no DNS of real hostnames)\n- Frontend (HIGH): Save button had onClick={handleSave} while also being\n  type=\"submit\" inside <form onSubmit>, firing the mutation twice. Remove\n  the onClick; the form onSubmit is the single trigger.\n- Frontend (HIGH): purge dialog focus was restored in both the finally\n  block and onClose; remove the finally focus so onClose is the single\n  source of truth.\n- A11y (MEDIUM): root <main> nested inside the Jahia shell''s <main>; use\n  <section aria-labelledby>. Add htmlFor to the project-name <output> and\n  an aria-describedby range hint to the batch-size input (en/de/fr).\n\n122 Java tests pass; Jest 16/16; SonarQube gate OK; Cypress 29 pass / 4 skip.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(security): close hex IPv4 SSRF bypass in isIpLiteral\n\nLoop-2 PR review found that hex IPv4 host forms (e.g. https://0x7f000001,\nwhich resolves to 127.0.0.1) escaped the SSRF guard: the ''x'' made isIpLiteral\nreturn false, so the host skipped the internal-IP range check and was treated\nas an opaque public hostname. Classify values whose segments start with 0x/0X\nas IP literals so they are range-checked (or fail safe on UnknownHostException).\nReal hostnames never start with 0x, so no genuine host is resolved. +2 tests.\n\n124 Java tests pass; SonarQube gate OK.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"7adfde36bbb34c009c9f6b8a56fd0e25cff918e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/7adfde36bbb34c009c9f6b8a56fd0e25cff918e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450","verification":{"payload":"tree 7adfde36bbb34c009c9f6b8a56fd0e25cff918e6\nparent cf485b8127cdf4ee68487895b6d0bbd3498a0eeb\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781897280 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781897280 +0200\n\nchore: harden customgpt-ai (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests) (#7)\n\n* chore: harden customgpt-ai (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests)\n\nBlind multi-level review (architecture, security, code quality, ergonomy,\naccessibility AAA, test coverage, documentation) and remediation.\n\nSecurity\n- SSRF guard: reject private/loopback/link-local/unique-local IP literals\n  for the CustomGPT API base URL and the page-render host (no DNS of\n  arbitrary hostnames); validate base URL is https in Config so bad .cfg\n  values cannot reach the HTTP layer carrying the Bearer token.\n- Explicit OkHttp connect/read/write/call timeouts on both clients.\n- GraphQL resolvers no longer leak internal exception detail to clients\n  (server-side log + generic message); audit-log admin actions\n  (saveSettings/startIndex/startNodeIndex/addSite/purgeAllPages) with the\n  sanitized acting user; validate addSite siteKey against ^[\\w-]+$.\n\nCorrectness / quality (Java)\n- Fix CustomGptIndexOperation equals/hashCode field-set mismatch that\n  corrupted LinkedHashSet de-duplication.\n- Thread-safety: volatile + synchronized executor restart, synchronized\n  init(); narrow broad catch(Exception); fix JCR event-type bit test\n  ((type & PROPERTY_EVENTS) != 0); remove dead code (duplicate ACE branch,\n  nodeToReindex map, write-only retryOnConflict, vacuous null guards);\n  hasProperty guard; lambdas for SAM callbacks; rename misspelled constants.\n\nFrontend / ergonomy\n- Remove console logging; one-time form init (drop Apollo onCompleted reset);\n  NaN guard + min/max on numeric inputs; client-side required-field\n  validation; name the GraphQL query and route/init functions.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA)\n- Native <output> polite live regions (deduped), dialog focus return,\n  aria-describedby hints, aria-invalid + inline errors, 24px touch targets,\n  AAA contrast, <form> semantics, prefers-reduced-motion, i18n parity (de/fr).\n\nTests\n- 22 -> 117 Java unit tests (RateLimitInterceptor, Indexer dedup, Config\n  parse, Service path predicate, SSRF guard) + 16 Jest/RTL tests.\n- Cypress: self-contained masking round-trip test, replace cy.wait(10000)\n  with polling, restore teardown, add saveSettings/purgeAllPages permission\n  deny tests.\n\nBuild / docs\n- Sync package.json version to pom (1.0.7-SNAPSHOT); add SonarQube\n  properties; correct AGENTS.md (React 18, pure OSGi DS).\n\nSonarQube quality gate: OK (0 new issues, ratings A, 0% duplication).\nCypress: 29 passing / 0 failing / 4 skipped (indexing specs need live creds).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review (SSRF dotless-IP bypass, double-submit, focus, landmark)\n\nBlind PR review findings:\n- Security (HIGH): SSRF guard bypass via dotless integer/decimal IPv4\n  literals (e.g. https://2130706433 -> 127.0.0.1, https://0 -> 0.0.0.0)\n  passed isHttpsUrl/isInternalHost because isIpLiteral required a dot.\n  Classify all-digit dotless values as IP literals so they are resolved\n  and range-checked; add tests. (no DNS of real hostnames)\n- Frontend (HIGH): Save button had onClick={handleSave} while also being\n  type=\"submit\" inside <form onSubmit>, firing the mutation twice. Remove\n  the onClick; the form onSubmit is the single trigger.\n- Frontend (HIGH): purge dialog focus was restored in both the finally\n  block and onClose; remove the finally focus so onClose is the single\n  source of truth.\n- A11y (MEDIUM): root <main> nested inside the Jahia shell''s <main>; use\n  <section aria-labelledby>. Add htmlFor to the project-name <output> and\n  an aria-describedby range hint to the batch-size input (en/de/fr).\n\n122 Java tests pass; Jest 16/16; SonarQube gate OK; Cypress 29 pass / 4 skip.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(security): close hex IPv4 SSRF bypass in isIpLiteral\n\nLoop-2 PR review found that hex IPv4 host forms (e.g. https://0x7f000001,\nwhich resolves to 127.0.0.1) escaped the SSRF guard: the ''x'' made isIpLiteral\nreturn false, so the host skipped the internal-IP range check and was treated\nas an opaque public hostname. Classify values whose segments start with 0x/0X\nas IP literals so they are range-checked (or fail safe on UnknownHostException).\nReal hostnames never start with 0x, so no genuine host is resolved. +2 tests.\n\n124 Java tests pass; SonarQube gate OK.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNZhACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAygoQAFie4OaG5ahGdQsacwoyPp8x\nK1WeZvXCVfz//sNGBxJTS7IvCmLhAP0M6Cg1Jm0DkclOWnfRnRfKP7LDpALNjW3b\nuNcBAC4qsDHyz9Q5BEMtiXTEfHUNlv8/YkoZtSBq4ZFyHLaYUZo8G5BOZKT9MnJP\ntUnExssjlHIQTCyE4M+xZWteYN0Tk/VfAKhtoMNeZc8sZ0BMMZFk4H/65OJBh+qM\nq7ik7wrqoOiVtZx+HSq97oncfruWRhAggg0XYyDpEoTUPT5Zsp7dGf3xRxvgKWvP\nEi0KRgbiIDdZN5E8e5Aei/Aj/UCqfjGtq5rWkWM6VJgRJxv1KHWQfZx53icUUZcS\nva2v+8sOy8NMJ9KqwTr4AdoZbN/fa3d5CM8DBLU9+ZJfFrJ/UkKHvoBae7Bu+iaM\nUMCuaqvwkuMqRq7E4MFBoTOK47Vi3dk1LwfWNk5gUFY+cPX+ecSBjYopfyvFWQHP\nqdiLvQKFKFCu+15/8DjD6KjwC8q4QS3e3PoJt+r/QbIJetNScpJNkysDfi20ZvJ0\nqFlbab3YqVqOYq5nseuxgAQGXFJKHRCD77hEWYX30uHHHIDtBRW/AxffBLPkx/l6\nbn7xp2y09slwWuN5qWJadSh0KJffzyxs7EnYKkL9MQ1A2cM4CVwYKpQbWzbmVmgL\nofhFMrONL5ASUVq1dD7M\n=qjZH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T19:28:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450","node_id":"C_kwDOOafN99oAKDg2YjRmMDg1ZDk3ZWM4YjcyMjlhYzBkMDA5ZDg5NGM2MTYyNjQ0NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commit/cf485b8127cdf4ee68487895b6d0bbd3498a0eeb","sha":"cf485b8127cdf4ee68487895b6d0bbd3498a0eeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/cf485b8127cdf4ee68487895b6d0bbd3498a0eeb"}],"sha":"86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/86b4f085d97ec8b7229ac0d009d894c616264450"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/commits/cf485b8127cdf4ee68487895b6d0bbd3498a0eeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#6)\n\n* test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role\n\nGuards the `customGptAdmin` permission gate across the stack against silent\nremoval or mismatch:\n\n- Backend: `@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"customGptAdmin\")` on the\n  `admin.customGpt` query/mutation extensions.\n- Frontend: `requiredPermission: ''customGptAdmin''` on the `customgptAiSettings`\n  admin route (register.jsx).\n\nChanges:\n- Add `src/main/import/roles.xml` shipping an assignable\n  `customgpt-ai-administrator` server role granting only\n  `administrationAccess customGptAdmin` (no full `admin`), so a user can reach\n  the CustomGPT.ai settings admin UI without server-administrator rights.\n- Add `tests/cypress/e2e/04-customGpt-Permissions.cy.ts` (4 tests): a user\n  granted ONLY the new role vs a user with no extra grant.\n  * GraphQL: denied user is rejected with \"Permission denied\"; the granted\n    user clears the `customGptAdmin` annotation gate.\n  * Admin UI: panel (\"CustomGPT.ai Settings\") hidden for the denied user,\n    visible for the granted user.\n- Bump module version 1.0.6-SNAPSHOT -> 1.0.7-SNAPSHOT so the new role import\n  content is re-imported on deploy.\n\nNote: every `admin.customGpt` resolver also performs a hardcoded\n`node(\"/\").hasPermission(\"admin\")` check on top of the field-level\n`customGptAdmin` annotation, so the GraphQL allow test asserts the granted user\nis not blocked by the fine-grained annotation gate rather than asserting a fully\nsuccessful resolver call. The inner global-`admin` check is a separate, broader\ngate that arguably makes the `customGptAdmin` annotation redundant for these\nresolvers — flagged for maintainer review.\n\nValidated: ./ci.build.sh && ./ci.startup.sh -> 31/31 specs pass, license health clean.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: relax inner admin check to customGptAdmin so the fine-grained role works end-to-end\n\nThe admin.customGpt GraphQL resolvers performed a hardcoded SERVER-level\ncheck checkAdminPermission(\"/\", \"admin\") in addition to the\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"customGptAdmin\") annotation. A user holding\nonly customGptAdmin cleared the annotation gate but was rejected at the\ndata layer by the inner global-admin check, making the fine-grained role\nunusable end-to-end.\n\nRename the constant ADMIN (\"admin\") to CUSTOM_GPT_ADMIN (\"customGptAdmin\")\nin AdminQueries and GqlCustomGptAdminMutationResult, so the root-path check\nmatches the annotation. Per-site checks keep PERM_SITE_ADMIN (\"site-admin\")\nand NodeReindexAsyncJob is untouched.\n\nUpdate the permission spec allow test to assert FULL success: the granted\nuser''s read-only getSettings query now returns data with no GraphQL errors.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"acba65c1debf993ebe9ca0284e35d4d107b9055f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/trees/acba65c1debf993ebe9ca0284e35d4d107b9055f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/customgpt-ai/git/commits/cf485b8127cdf4ee68487895b6d0bbd3498a0eeb","verification":{"payload":"tree acba65c1debf993ebe9ca0284e35d4d107b9055f\nparent 295bd2aad88efb13ded32921cf109d4fe71f939c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118405 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118405 +0200\n\ntest: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#6)\n\n* test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role\n\nGuards the `customGptAdmin` permission gate across the stack against silent\nremoval or mismatch:\n\n- Backend: `@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"customGptAdmin\")` on the\n  `admin.customGpt` query/mutation extensions.\n- Frontend: `requiredPermission: ''customGptAdmin''` on the `customgptAiSettings`\n  admin route (register.jsx).\n\nChanges:\n- Add `src/main/import/roles.xml` shipping an assignable\n  `customgpt-ai-administrator` server role granting only\n  `administrationAccess customGptAdmin` (no full `admin`), so a user can reach\n  the CustomGPT.ai settings admin UI without server-administrator rights.\n- Add `tests/cypress/e2e/04-customGpt-Permissions.cy.ts` (4 tests): a user\n  granted ONLY the new role vs a user with no extra grant.\n  * GraphQL: denied user is rejected with \"Permission denied\"; the granted\n    user clears the `customGptAdmin` annotation gate.\n  * Admin UI: panel (\"CustomGPT.ai Settings\") hidden for the denied user,\n    visible for the granted user.\n- Bump module version 1.0.6-SNAPSHOT -> 1.0.7-SNAPSHOT so the new role import\n  content is re-imported on deploy.\n\nNote: every `admin.customGpt` resolver also performs a hardcoded\n`node(\"/\").hasPermission(\"admin\")` check on top of the field-level\n`customGptAdmin` annotation, so the GraphQL allow test asserts the granted user\nis not blocked by the fine-grained annotation gate rather than asserting a fully\nsuccessful resolver call. The inner global-`admin` check is a separate, broader\ngate that arguably makes the `customGptAdmin` annotation redundant for these\nresolvers — flagged for maintainer review.\n\nValidated: ./ci.build.sh && ./ci.startup.sh -> 31/31 specs pass, license health clean.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: relax inner admin check to customGptAdmin so the fine-grained role works end-to-end\n\nThe admin.customGpt GraphQL resolvers performed a hardcoded SERVER-level\ncheck checkAdminPermission(\"/\", \"admin\") in addition to the\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"customGptAdmin\") annotation. A user holding\nonly customGptAdmin cleared the annotation gate but was rejected at the\ndata layer by the inner global-admin check, making the fine-grained role\nunusable end-to-end.\n\nRename the constant ADMIN (\"admin\") to CUSTOM_GPT_ADMIN (\"customGptAdmin\")\nin AdminQueries and GqlCustomGptAdminMutationResult, so the root-path check\nmatches the annotation. Per-site checks keep PERM_SITE_ADMIN (\"site-admin\")\nand NodeReindexAsyncJob is untouched.\n\nUpdate the permission spec allow test to assert FULL success: the granted\nuser''s read-only getSettings query now returns data with no GraphQL errors.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbXFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArVwQAJof+phUPFGqFzHAIKlJ+l7d\nNh5EAOWfLz8MizhhN8oxCu6BpPyAnxO+6LR8N1DkFk2w2+SKkySbB+uaE5D/lwC8\n4JTc5sQvCwaLBr691Oo+makkUzDPCH+JtPmAwTugQThFgHQy9sMGTXSwx308BdOS\na8eNldm5EUDlHW6JOGY5wfvEGelMpOi/gtMBCZfJY4C24vYxEXr8oLA1XbQVdvmo\n03Vmh8zRjoXpVNMoZbyIzzY+KNYc3MT2uBUruT9AIQePm0nRwpDU/kDYm9cw14cY\nm86XFPxYY/3B5H0TJvwcMYZ2D2Ltep+5ap1c8d/PUgdmlHhUe3npBE6uB+YiRQBN\nGxV7lLmNuJQJzoZfal1WArObAmZtfqW7IxNqyh7RU7p7xOP8ASs3pJgKaLpwZysq\n3oR2irVtnnuU8dCWh4Y0u